DGAlgebras -- Data types and basic functions on differential graded (DG) Algebras.
**********************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package is used to define and manipulate DG algebras.

Contributors
============

Some documentation was added by Daniel Rostamloo and David Eisenbud.

* Menu:

* Basic operations on DG Algebras::  Outlines some basic operations on DG Algebras
* The Koszul complex as a DG Algebra::  an example
* Basic operations on DG Algebra Maps::  Outlines some basic operations on DGAlgebraMaps
* Basic operations on DG Module Maps::  Outlines some basic operations on DGModuleMaps
* Base change and tensor with non-DG types::  Tensoring DG objects with ordinary rings and modules
* Operations on DG Ideals::     Sum, product, power, intersection, colon, and other ideal-algebra operations on DG ideals
* Building DG modules, submodules, and quotients: Building DG modules_cm submodules_cm and quotients.  The DGModule / DGSubmodule / DGQuotientModule hierarchy and its constructors
* Module-like operations on DG modules::  Basic queries (generators, rank, degrees, homogeneity) extended to DG modules and their sub- and quotient modules
* Operations on DG Submodules::  Sum, intersection, equality, and containment of DG submodules
* Image, kernel, and cokernel of DG module maps: Image_cm kernel_cm and cokernel of DG module maps.  Building DG submodules and DG quotient modules from a DG module map
* Homology of DG modules and DG module maps::  Computing H_n and H_* for DG modules, DG submodules, DG quotient modules, and DG module maps
* Pruning DG modules, submodules, quotients, and maps: Pruning DG modules_cm submodules_cm quotients_cm and maps.  Minimizing presentations of DG types via prune and minimalPresentation
* Well-definedness, acyclicity, and quasi-isomorphism: Well-definedness_cm acyclicity_cm and quasi-isomorphism.  Predicates that check DG-theoretic conditions on DG types
* Semifree resolutions of DG modules::  Building semifree DG module resolutions via koszulComplexDGM, adjoinGenerators, killCycles, and semifreeResolution
* Computing module differentials and visualizing DG modules::  Differential matrices, element-wise differentials, and visualization helpers for DG modules
* Building DG algebras from existing DG algebras::  Base change, generator restriction, truncation, and targeted cycle-killing for DG algebras
* Low-level differential computations and validity checks::  Primitives behind DG algebra and DG module differentials
* Accessors and cache management::  Reading state out of a DG algebra or DG module and maintaining its caches
* DG module primitives and chain-complex export::  Installing differentials, reading degree data, and exporting to Complex

