DGModule ** Ring -- Base change of a DG module along a ring map
***************************************************************

  * Operator: *note **: (Macaulay2Doc)_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        MS = M ** S
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A (free) DG
        module over some DG algebra A.
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, A ring admitting substitution
        from A.ring.  Typically S = A.ring / I.
  * Outputs:
      * MS, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A DG module over
        A ** S with the same generator multi-degrees as M and with differential
        obtained by substituting every entry of each differential column into
        the base-changed algebra.

Description
===========

This is the base change of M along the ring map A.ring -> S, lifted to the DG
level.  Since A ** S and M ** S are both cached, repeated tensoring with S is
idempotent up to object identity:

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y]                        |
|                                            |
|o1 = R                                      |
|                                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                         |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                 |
|                                            |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }  |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]   |
|                               1,1   1,2    |
|      Differential => {x, y}                |
|                                            |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                              |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0, 1})            |
|                                            |
|o3 = {Base ring => R                       }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]           |
|                       1,1   1,2            |
|                                       2    |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])     |
|                            1,1   1,2       |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 0}} |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, 0}       |
|                                            |
|o3 : DGModule                               |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : QR = R / ideal(x^2)                    |
|                                            |
|o4 = QR                                     |
|                                            |
|o4 : QuotientRing                           |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : MS = M ** QR                           |
|                                            |
|o5 = {Base ring => QR                      }|
|      DG algebra => QR[T   ..T   ]          |
|                        1,1   1,2           |
|                                        2   |
|      Natural module => (QR[T   ..T   ])    |
|                             1,1   1,2      |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 0}} |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, 0}       |
|                                            |
|o5 : DGModule                               |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : MS === M ** QR                         |
|                                            |
|o6 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i7 : MS.dgAlgebra === A ** QR               |
|                                            |
|o7 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isWellDefined MS                       |
|                                            |
|o8 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

When M is the Koszul complex on a sequence and the map A.ring -> S is a
quotient map, M ** S is the Koszul complex of the same sequence computed over
S.

See also
========

  * *note Base change and tensor with non-DG types: Base change and tensor with
    non-DG types, -- Tensoring DG objects with ordinary rings and modules
  * *note DGAlgebra ** Ring: DGAlgebra _st_st Ring, -- Base change of a DG
    algebra to another ring
  * *note DGModuleMap ** Ring: DGModuleMap _st_st Ring, -- Base change of a DG
    module map along a ring map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note DGModule ** Ring: DGModule _st_st Ring, -- Base change of a DG module
    along a ring map
