DGAlgebraMap ** Ring -- Base change of a DG algebra map along a ring map
************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note **: (Macaulay2Doc)_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        phiS = phi ** S
  * Inputs:
      * phi, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap,, A DG
        algebra map A -> B.
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * phiS, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap,, A DG
        algebra map A ** S -> B ** S whose underlying RingMap sends each
        generator of A.natural to the image under phi, substituted into (B **
        S).natural.

Description
===========

Functorial and compatible with object identity: because A ** S and B ** S are
cached, repeated evaluations of phi ** S land in the same source/target, and
identityDGAlgebraMap(A) ** S equals identityDGAlgebraMap(A ** S).

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y]                                         |
|                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                       |
|                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                  |
|                                                             |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                   |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                    |
|                               1,1   1,2                     |
|      Differential => {x, y}                                 |
|                                                             |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : idA = identityDGAlgebraMap A                            |
|                                                             |
|o3 = map (R[T   ..T   ], R[T   ..T   ], {T   , T   , x, y})  |
|             1,1   1,2      1,1   1,2     1,1   1,2          |
|                                                             |
|o3 : DGAlgebraMap                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : QR = R / ideal(x^2)                                     |
|                                                             |
|o4 = QR                                                      |
|                                                             |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : idAQ = idA ** QR                                        |
|                                                             |
|o5 = map (QR[T   ..T   ], QR[T   ..T   ], {T   , T   , x, y})|
|              1,1   1,2       1,1   1,2     1,1   1,2        |
|                                                             |
|o5 : DGAlgebraMap                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isWellDefined idAQ                                      |
|                                                             |
|o6 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : (idAQ.source) === (A ** QR)                             |
|                                                             |
|o7 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : (idAQ.target) === (A ** QR)                             |
|                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Base change and tensor with non-DG types: Base change and tensor with
    non-DG types, -- Tensoring DG objects with ordinary rings and modules
  * *note DGAlgebra ** Ring: DGAlgebra _st_st Ring, -- Base change of a DG
    algebra to another ring
  * *note identityDGAlgebraMap: identityDGAlgebraMap, -- The identity
    DGAlgebraMap on a DG algebra

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note DGAlgebraMap ** Ring: DGAlgebraMap _st_st Ring, -- Base change of a
    DG algebra map along a ring map
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

