DGSubmodule ** Module -- Exterior tensor product of a DG submodule with an ordinary free module
***********************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note **: (Macaulay2Doc)_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        SubN = Sub ** N
        SubN = N ** Sub
  * Inputs:
      * Sub, an instance of the type *note DGSubmodule: DGSubmodule,, 
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, A free module over a
        compatible ring.
  * Outputs:
      * SubN, an instance of the type *note DGSubmodule: DGSubmodule,, The DG
        submodule of (Sub.ambient) ** N whose inclusion acts as inclusion(Sub)
        \otimes id_N on natural generators indexed by (i, j).

Description
===========

Equivalently: for each natural generator of N, embed a copy of Sub's inclusion
matrix into the corresponding block of the tensored ambient. The commuted form
N ** Sub is defined as Sub ** N.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y]                                |
|                                                    |
|o1 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                         |
|                                                    |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }          |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]           |
|                               1,1   1,2            |
|      Differential => {x, y}                        |
|                                                    |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Anat = A.natural                               |
|                                                    |
|o3 = Anat                                           |
|                                                    |
|o3 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s) |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0})                       |
|                                                    |
|o4 = {Base ring => R               }                |
|      DG algebra => Anat                            |
|                            1                       |
|      Natural module => Anat                        |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}                 |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}                  |
|                                                    |
|o4 : DGModule                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Sub = dgSubmodule(M, matrix {{x_Anat, y_Anat}})|
|                                                    |
|o5 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule                |
|     Degrees  => {{0, 1}, {0, 1}}                   |
|                     2                              |
|     natural  => Anat                               |
|     inclusion => | x y |                           |
|                                                    |
|o5 : DGSubmodule                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : N = R^2                                        |
|                                                    |
|      2                                             |
|o6 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o6 : R-module, free                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : SubN = Sub ** N                                |
|                                                    |
|o7 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule                |
|     Degrees  => {{0, 1}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}}   |
|                     4                              |
|     natural  => Anat                               |
|     inclusion => | x 0 y 0 |                       |
|                  | 0 x 0 y |                       |
|                                                    |
|o7 : DGSubmodule                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isWellDefined SubN                             |
|                                                    |
|o8 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : SubN.ambient === M ** N                        |
|                                                    |
|o9 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Base change and tensor with non-DG types: Base change and tensor with
    non-DG types, -- Tensoring DG objects with ordinary rings and modules
  * *note DGModule ** Module: DGModule _st_st Module, -- Exterior tensor
    product of a DG module with an ordinary free module
  * *note DGSubmodule ** Ring: DGSubmodule _st_st Ring, -- Base change of a DG
    submodule along a ring map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note DGSubmodule ** Module: DGSubmodule _st_st Module, -- Exterior tensor
    product of a DG submodule with an ordinary free module
  * "Module ** DGSubmodule"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

