isDGIdeal -- Test whether an ideal of A.natural is closed under the differential of A
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isDGIdeal(A, I)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, An ideal of A.natural.
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, True iff every
        minimal generator g of I satisfies polyDifferential(A, g) % I == 0.

Description
===========

Unlike *note dgIdeal: dgIdeal, (which d-saturates), isDGIdeal simply checks
d-closure without modifying the input.  Use it to validate that an
externally-produced Ideal is already a DG ideal.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y]                                       |
|                                                            |
|o1 = R                                                      |
|                                                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                 |
|                                                            |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                  |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                   |
|                               1,1   1,2                    |
|      Differential => {x, y}                                |
|                                                            |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Anat = A.natural                                       |
|                                                            |
|o3 = Anat                                                   |
|                                                            |
|o3 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s)         |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isDGIdeal(A, ideal(x_Anat, y_Anat))                    |
|                                                            |
|o4 = true                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T = Anat_0   -- first Koszul variable T_{1,1}; d(T) = x|
|                                                            |
|o5 = T                                                      |
|      1,1                                                   |
|                                                            |
|o5 : Anat                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isDGIdeal(A, ideal(T))                                 |
|                                                            |
|o6 = false                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

The second test returns false: the ideal (T) is not d-closed because d(T) = x
is not in it.  Passing the same seed to *note dgIdeal: dgIdeal, produces the
d-closure.

+--------------------------------+
|i7 : J = dgIdeal(A, {T})        |
|                                |
|o7 = DGIdeal of Anat            |
|     generators => | x T_(1,1) ||
|                                |
|o7 : DGIdeal                    |
+--------------------------------+
|i8 : isDGIdeal(A, J.natural)    |
|                                |
|o8 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+

