DGIdeal + DGIdeal -- Sum of two DG ideals
*****************************************

  * Operator: *note +: (Macaulay2Doc)+,
  * Usage: 
        K = I + J
  * Inputs:
      * I, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, 
      * J, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, With I.dgAlgebra
        === J.dgAlgebra.
  * Outputs:
      * K, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, The DGIdeal with
        K.natural = I.natural + J.natural.

Description
===========

Preserves d-closure because d(I + J) \subset dI + dJ \subset I + J.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y]                              |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                        |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }         |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]          |
|                               1,1   1,2           |
|      Differential => {x, y}                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Anat = A.natural                              |
|                                                   |
|o3 = Anat                                          |
|                                                   |
|o3 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = dgIdeal(A, {x_Anat})                      |
|                                                   |
|o4 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | x |                           |
|                                                   |
|o4 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : J = dgIdeal(A, {y_Anat})                      |
|                                                   |
|o5 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | y |                           |
|                                                   |
|o5 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : K = I + J                                     |
|                                                   |
|o6 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | y x |                         |
|                                                   |
|o6 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined K                               |
|                                                   |
|o7 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : (I + J) == (J + I)                            |
|                                                   |
|o8 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

The zero DGIdeal is a two-sided identity for +.

+-----------------------+
|i9 : Z = dgIdeal(A, {})|
|                       |
|o9 = DGIdeal of Anat   |
|     generators => 0   |
|                       |
|o9 : DGIdeal           |
+-----------------------+
|i10 : (Z + I) == I     |
|                       |
|o10 = true             |
+-----------------------+

