DGIdeal * DGIdeal -- Product of two DG ideals
*********************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        K = I * J
  * Inputs:
      * I, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, 
      * J, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, With I.dgAlgebra
        === J.dgAlgebra.
  * Outputs:
      * K, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, The DGIdeal with
        K.natural = I.natural * J.natural.

Description
===========

Preserves d-closure by the Leibniz rule: d(ab) = d(a) b \pm a d(b) shows d(IJ)
\subset (dI) J + I (dJ) \subset IJ.  When the ambient ring is commutative,
multiplication is commutative.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y]                              |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                        |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }         |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]          |
|                               1,1   1,2           |
|      Differential => {x, y}                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Anat = A.natural                              |
|                                                   |
|o3 = Anat                                          |
|                                                   |
|o3 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = dgIdeal(A, {x_Anat})                      |
|                                                   |
|o4 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | x |                           |
|                                                   |
|o4 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : J = dgIdeal(A, {y_Anat})                      |
|                                                   |
|o5 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | y |                           |
|                                                   |
|o5 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : K = I * J                                     |
|                                                   |
|o6 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | xy |                          |
|                                                   |
|o6 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined K                               |
|                                                   |
|o7 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : (I * J) == (J * I)                            |
|                                                   |
|o8 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

The unit DGIdeal is a two-sided identity for * (as ideals).

+-----------------------------+
|i9 : U = dgIdeal(A, {1_Anat})|
|                             |
|o9 = DGIdeal of Anat         |
|     generators => | 1 |     |
|                             |
|o9 : DGIdeal                 |
+-----------------------------+
|i10 : (U * I) == I           |
|                             |
|o10 = true                   |
+-----------------------------+

