intersect(DGIdeal,DGIdeal) -- Intersection of two DG ideals
***********************************************************

  * Function: *note intersect: (Macaulay2Doc)intersect,
  * Usage: 
        K = intersect(I, J)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, 
      * J, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, With I.dgAlgebra
        === J.dgAlgebra.
  * Outputs:
      * K, an instance of the type *note DGIdeal: DGIdeal,, The DGIdeal with
        K.natural = intersect(I.natural, J.natural).

Description
===========

Intersections preserve d-closure directly: if g lies in both I and J, then d(g)
lies in both (by d-closure of each), hence in their intersection.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y]                              |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                        |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }         |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]          |
|                               1,1   1,2           |
|      Differential => {x, y}                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Anat = A.natural                              |
|                                                   |
|o3 = Anat                                          |
|                                                   |
|o3 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = dgIdeal(A, {x_Anat})                      |
|                                                   |
|o4 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | x |                           |
|                                                   |
|o4 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : J = dgIdeal(A, {y_Anat})                      |
|                                                   |
|o5 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | y |                           |
|                                                   |
|o5 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : K = intersect(I, J)                           |
|                                                   |
|o6 = DGIdeal of Anat                               |
|     generators => | xy |                          |
|                                                   |
|o6 : DGIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined K                               |
|                                                   |
|o7 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Intersecting with the zero DGIdeal yields the zero DGIdeal.

+-----------------------------+
|i8 : Z = dgIdeal(A, {})      |
|                             |
|o8 = DGIdeal of Anat         |
|     generators => 0         |
|                             |
|o8 : DGIdeal                 |
+-----------------------------+
|i9 : ZI = intersect(Z, I)    |
|                             |
|o9 = DGIdeal of Anat         |
|     generators => 0         |
|                             |
|o9 : DGIdeal                 |
+-----------------------------+
|i10 : isWellDefined ZI       |
|                             |
|o10 = true                   |
+-----------------------------+
|i11 : numgens ZI.natural == 0|
|                             |
|o11 = true                   |
+-----------------------------+

