dgQuotientModule -- Construct the quotient DG module M / S
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Q = dgQuotientModule(M, S)
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
      * S, an instance of the type *note DGSubmodule: DGSubmodule,, With
        S.ambient === M.
  * Outputs:
      * Q, an instance of the type *note DGQuotientModule: DGQuotientModule,,
        The cokernel of S.inclusion.natural equipped with the induced
        differential.

Description
===========

The shorthand M / S calls this constructor.  The resulting Q records the
ambient M (via *note ambient: (Macaulay2Doc)ambient,), the killed submodule S
(via *note subDGModule: ambient,), and the quotient map M → Q (via *note
projection: ambient,).

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x]                  |
|                                    |
|o1 = R                              |
|                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                 |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R         |
|                                    |
|o2 = {Ring => R                    }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ] |
|                               1,1  |
|      Differential => {x}           |
|                                    |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                      |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0})       |
|                                    |
|o3 = {Base ring => R               }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ]         |
|                       1,1          |
|                                 1  |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ])   |
|                            1,1     |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}} |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}  |
|                                    |
|o3 : DGModule                       |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : Z = dgSubmodule(M, {})         |
|                                    |
|o4 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule|
|     Degrees  => {}                 |
|     natural  => 0                  |
|     inclusion => 0                 |
|                                    |
|o4 : DGSubmodule                    |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : Q = dgQuotientModule(M, Z)     |
|                                    |
|o5 = DGQuotientModule Q = M / S     |
|                          1         |
|     Q.natural = (R[T   ])          |
|                     1,1            |
|     Degrees   = {{0, 0}}           |
|                                    |
|o5 : DGQuotientModule               |
+------------------------------------+
|i6 : instance(Q, DGQuotientModule)  |
|                                    |
|o6 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i7 : ambient Q === M                |
|                                    |
|o7 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i8 : subDGModule Q === Z            |
|                                    |
|o8 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+

Quotienting by the zero submodule gives a DGQuotientModule whose underlying
cokernel is isomorphic to M.natural; quotienting by the whole ambient yields
the zero DGQuotientModule.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Sfull = dgSubmodule(M, id_(M.natural))|
|                                           |
|o9 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule       |
|     Degrees  => {{0, 0}}                  |
|                          1                |
|     natural  => (R[T   ])                 |
|                     1,1                   |
|     inclusion => | 1 |                    |
|                                           |
|o9 : DGSubmodule                           |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i10 : Qzero = M / Sfull                    |
|                                           |
|o10 = DGQuotientModule Q = M / S           |
|      Q.natural = cokernel | 1 |           |
|      Degrees   = {{0, 0}}                 |
|                                           |
|o10 : DGQuotientModule                     |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i11 : isZero Qzero                         |
|                                           |
|o11 = true                                 |
+-------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

S.ambient must equal M as an object (===), not merely be isomorphic.  This
enforces a strict lattice-of-submodules discipline on the resulting quotient.

See also
========

  * *note Building DG modules, submodules, and quotients: Building DG
    modules_cm submodules_cm and quotients, -- The DGModule / DGSubmodule /
    DGQuotientModule hierarchy and its constructors
  * *note DGModule / DGSubmodule: DGModule / DGSubmodule, -- Quotient DG
    module: M / S
  * *note DGQuotientModule: DGQuotientModule, -- The class of quotient DG
    modules M / S
  * *note projection: ambient, -- Accessors for the ambient object, inclusion,
    projection, and killed submodule
  * *note subDGModule: ambient, -- Accessors for the ambient object, inclusion,
    projection, and killed submodule

Ways to use dgQuotientModule:
=============================

  * "dgQuotientModule(DGModule,DGSubmodule)"

For the programmer
==================

