rank(DGModule) -- Rank of the underlying free A.natural-module
**************************************************************

  * Function: *note rank: (Macaulay2Doc)rank,
  * Usage: 
        r = rank M
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A DGModule or
        DGSubmodule whose .natural is free.
  * Outputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, rank M.natural.

Description
===========

For a free DGModule, rank and *note numgens: (Macaulay2Doc)numgens, coincide.
For a DGSubmodule, rank reports the rank of the included free module (which is
numgens S when the inclusion is injective on natural generators — always the
case for submodules built by *note dgSubmodule: dgSubmodule,).

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y]                              |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                        |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }         |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]          |
|                               1,1   1,2           |
|      Differential => {x, y}                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0, 1})                   |
|                                                   |
|o3 = {Base ring => R                       }       |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                  |
|                       1,1   1,2                   |
|                                       2           |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])            |
|                            1,1   1,2              |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 0}}        |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, 0}              |
|                                                   |
|o3 : DGModule                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rank M == numgens M                           |
|                                                   |
|o4 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Anat = A.natural                              |
|                                                   |
|o5 = Anat                                          |
|                                                   |
|o5 : PolynomialRing, 2 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M1 = freeDGModule(A, {0})                     |
|                                                   |
|o6 = {Base ring => R               }               |
|      DG algebra => Anat                           |
|                            1                      |
|      Natural module => Anat                       |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}                |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}                 |
|                                                   |
|o6 : DGModule                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = dgSubmodule(M1, matrix {{x_Anat, y_Anat}})|
|                                                   |
|o7 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule               |
|     Degrees  => {{0, 1}, {0, 1}}                  |
|                     2                             |
|     natural  => Anat                              |
|     inclusion => | x y |                          |
|                                                   |
|o7 : DGSubmodule                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : rank S                                        |
|                                                   |
|o8 = 2                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+

After pruning a DGSubmodule with redundant inclusions, rank equals numgens on
the pruned object.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Sbig = dgSubmodule(M1, matrix {{1_Anat, x_Anat, y_Anat}})|
|                                                              |
|o9 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule                          |
|     Degrees  => {{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}}                     |
|                     3                                        |
|     natural  => Anat                                         |
|     inclusion => | 1 x y |                                   |
|                                                              |
|o9 : DGSubmodule                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : Sp = prune Sbig                                         |
|                                                              |
|o10 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule                         |
|      Degrees  => {{0, 0}}                                    |
|                      1                                       |
|      natural  => Anat                                        |
|      inclusion => | 1 |                                      |
|                                                              |
|o10 : DGSubmodule                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : numgens Sp == rank Sp                                   |
|                                                              |
|o11 = true                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

rank is not defined on *note DGQuotientModule: DGQuotientModule,: the rank of a
cokernel module triggers codim computations that fail over non-affine graded
ambients.  Use *note numgens: (Macaulay2Doc)numgens, for the generator count.

See also
========

  * *note Module-like operations on DG modules: Module-like operations on DG
    modules, -- Basic queries (generators, rank, degrees, homogeneity) extended
    to DG modules and their sub- and quotient modules
  * *note numgens(DGModule): numgens_lpDGModule_rp, -- Number of natural
    generators of a DG module (or sub- or quotient module)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note rank(DGModule): rank_lpDGModule_rp, -- Rank of the underlying free
    A.natural-module
  * "rank(DGSubmodule)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

