prune(DGModule) -- Pruning a DG module is the identity
******************************************************

  * Function: *note prune: (Macaulay2Doc)prune,
  * Usage: 
        Mp = prune M
        Mp = minimalPresentation M
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Exclude: (Macaulay2Doc)minimalPresentation_lpRing_rp, => ...,
        default value {},
  * Outputs:
      * Mp, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, The same DG
        module M.  A pruningMap equal to the identity DG module map on M is
        cached in M.cache.

Description
===========

DG modules as stored in this package (built from *note freeDGModule:
freeDGModule, or *note koszulComplexDGM: koszulComplexDGM,) carry no auxiliary
presentation data that prune could minimize; the method is installed as the
identity so that calling code can use prune uniformly across DG types.

Calling prune M has the side effect of caching an identity *note DGModuleMap:
DGModuleMap, under the symbol pruningMap in M.cache.

minimalPresentation is a synonym for prune.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x]                          |
|                                            |
|o1 = R                                      |
|                                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                         |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                 |
|                                            |
|o2 = {Ring => R                    }        |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ]         |
|                               1,1          |
|      Differential => {x}                   |
|                                            |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                              |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0, 1})            |
|                                            |
|o3 = {Base ring => R                       }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ]                 |
|                       1,1                  |
|                                 2          |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ])           |
|                            1,1             |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 0}} |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, 0}       |
|                                            |
|o3 : DGModule                               |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (prune M) === M                        |
|                                            |
|o4 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : (minimalPresentation M) === M          |
|                                            |
|o5 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

