Well-definedness, acyclicity, and quasi-isomorphism -- Predicates that check DG-theoretic conditions on DG types
****************************************************************************************************************

The package exposes three families of predicates for checking conditions that
distinguish DG objects from their underlying graded / module-theoretic data.

*note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined, — verifies that an object
satisfies the DG axioms appropriate to its type.  For a *note DGAlgebra:
DGAlgebra, or *note DGModule: DGModule,, the central check is that the stored
differential squares to zero on every generator.  For a *note DGSubmodule:
DGSubmodule, or *note DGQuotientModule: DGQuotientModule,, the check is
d-closure of the defining submodule; for a *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap, or
*note DGModuleMap: DGModuleMap,, the check is the chain-map condition d \circ f
= f \circ d on every generator.

*note isAcyclic: isAcyclic, — returns true when a DG algebra or DG module has
H_i = 0 for all i >= 1 up to a finite bound.  For objects with infinite
hom-degree the user must supply *note EndDegree: EndDegree,.

*note isQuasiIsomorphism: (Complexes)isQuasiIsomorphism_lpComplexMap_rp, —
returns true when a DG algebra map or DG module map induces an isomorphism on
H_*.  The underlying check is performed on *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap,
and inherits the Concentration option from the Complexes package.

All three predicates accept the option *note EndDegree: EndDegree, where
applicable; for finite-degree objects the default bound is maxDegree of the
object and no option is required.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z]                               |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                        |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }         |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]          |
|                               1,1   1,3           |
|      Differential => {x, y, z}                    |
|                                                   |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isWellDefined A                               |
|                                                   |
|o3 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isAcyclic A                                   |
|                                                   |
|o4 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Anat = A.natural                              |
|                                                   |
|o5 = Anat                                          |
|                                                   |
|o5 : PolynomialRing, 3 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0})                      |
|                                                   |
|o6 = {Base ring => R               }               |
|      DG algebra => Anat                           |
|                            1                      |
|      Natural module => Anat                       |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}                |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}                 |
|                                                   |
|o6 : DGModule                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = dgSubmodule(M, matrix {{1_Anat}})         |
|                                                   |
|o7 = DGSubmodule of ambient DGModule               |
|     Degrees  => {{0, 0}}                          |
|                     1                             |
|     natural  => Anat                              |
|     inclusion => | 1 |                            |
|                                                   |
|o7 : DGSubmodule                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Q = M / S                                     |
|                                                   |
|o8 = DGQuotientModule Q = M / S                    |
|     Q.natural = cokernel | 1 |                    |
|     Degrees   = {{0, 0}}                          |
|                                                   |
|o8 : DGQuotientModule                              |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isWellDefined S                               |
|                                                   |
|o9 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : isWellDefined Q                              |
|                                                   |
|o10 = true                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : phi = identityDGAlgebraMap A                 |
|                                                   |
|o11 = map (Anat, Anat, {T   , T   , T   , x, y, z})|
|                         1,1   1,2   1,3           |
|                                                   |
|o11 : DGAlgebraMap                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : isWellDefined phi                            |
|                                                   |
|o12 = true                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : isQuasiIsomorphism phi                       |
|                                                   |
|o13 = true                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+

For a regular polynomial ring the Koszul DG algebra is acyclic and its identity
map is a quasi-isomorphism.  Both S and Q = M / S are well-defined because S is
d-closed.

