isWellDefined(DGAlgebra) -- Check that a DG algebra has correct structure and a differential that squares to zero
*****************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        b = isWellDefined A
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, True when A has all
        expected structural keys with the correct types, the base ring of
        A.natural is compatible with A.ring, the differential lowers
        homological degree by one on every generator, and d^2 = 0 holds on
        every generator of A.natural.

Description
===========

Checks three conditions in order.  First, a structural validation: the DG
algebra has keys ring, natural, diff, and Degrees with the right types, and the
length of A.Degrees equals the number of generators of A.natural.  Second,
every generator g of A.natural has d(g) of homological degree |g| - 1.  Third,
d^2(g) = 0 on every generator — Leibniz then extends this to all of A.natural.

When debugLevel > 0 the routine prints a diagnostic line for each failing
check.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z]                      |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R               |
|                                          |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,3  |
|      Differential => {x, y, z}           |
|                                          |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isWellDefined A                      |
|                                          |
|o3 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

A DG algebra with A.diff == {} (no differential set) passes the check trivially
— the second and third conditions apply only to generators with a stored
differential.

See also
========

  * *note Well-definedness, acyclicity, and quasi-isomorphism:
    Well-definedness_cm acyclicity_cm and quasi-isomorphism, -- Predicates that
    check DG-theoretic conditions on DG types
  * *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra, -- The class of all DGAlgebras
  * *note setDiff: setDiff, -- Install or replace the differential on a DG
    algebra
  * *note isWellDefined(DGIdeal): isWellDefined_lpDGIdeal_rp, -- Verify that a
    DGIdeal has correct structure and is d-closed
  * *note isAcyclic(DGAlgebra): isAcyclic, -- Determine whether a DG algebra
    has no higher homology

