isAcyclic(DGModule) -- Determine whether a DG module has vanishing positive-degree homology
*******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isAcyclic: isAcyclic,
  * Usage: 
        b = isAcyclic M
        b = isAcyclic(M, EndDegree => n)
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note EndDegree: isAcyclic_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => an
        *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value -1, An upper bound for
        the range of degrees checked.  Required when M has infinite *note
        maxDegree: maxDegree, (for example, when its DG algebra is an *note
        acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure,).  When omitted and M is
        finite-dimensional, maxDegree M is used.
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, True when H_i(M) = 0
        for all 1 <= i <= n.

Description
===========

Checks per-degree homology via *note HH_ZZ DGModule: HH_usZZ DGModule, and
*note prune: (Macaulay2Doc)prune,.  Degree zero is intentionally excluded:
acyclicity concerns only positive-degree homology.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z]                      |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R               |
|                                          |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,3  |
|      Differential => {x, y, z}           |
|                                          |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : KM = koszulComplexDGM R^1            |
|                                          |
|o3 = {Base ring => R                    } |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]         |
|                       1,1   1,3          |
|                                       1  |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])   |
|                            1,1   1,3     |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}       |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}        |
|                                          |
|o3 : DGModule                             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isAcyclic KM                         |
|                                          |
|o4 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

For the Koszul DG module on a regular sequence, all positive-degree homology
vanishes (H_0 = R / (x, y, z) is the only nonzero piece).

+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R' = QQ[x, y]/ideal(x^2, y^2)        |
|                                          |
|o5 = R'                                   |
|                                          |
|o5 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : KM' = koszulComplexDGM R'^1          |
|                                          |
|o6 = {Base ring => R'                    }|
|      DG algebra => R'[T   ..T   ]        |
|                        1,1   1,2         |
|                                        1 |
|      Natural module => (R'[T   ..T   ])  |
|                             1,1   1,2    |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}       |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}        |
|                                          |
|o6 : DGModule                             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : not isAcyclic(KM', EndDegree => 3)   |
|                                          |
|o7 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

Over a non-regular ring the Koszul DG module picks up nontrivial
positive-degree homology.

See also
========

  * *note Well-definedness, acyclicity, and quasi-isomorphism:
    Well-definedness_cm acyclicity_cm and quasi-isomorphism, -- Predicates that
    check DG-theoretic conditions on DG types
  * *note isAcyclic(DGAlgebra): isAcyclic, -- Determine whether a DG algebra
    has no higher homology
  * *note isAcyclic(DGQuotientModule): isAcyclic_lpDGQuotientModule_rp, --
    Determine whether a DG quotient module has vanishing positive-degree
    homology
  * *note HH_ZZ DGModule: HH_usZZ DGModule, -- The degree-n homology of a DG
    module as a module over the base ring
  * *note EndDegree: EndDegree, -- Option to specify the last homological
    degree processed by an iterative DG construction

