isQuasiIsomorphism(DGAlgebraMap) -- Determine whether a DG algebra map induces an isomorphism on homology
*********************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isQuasiIsomorphism:
    (Complexes)isQuasiIsomorphism_lpComplexMap_rp,
  * Usage: 
        b = isQuasiIsomorphism phi
  * Inputs:
      * phi, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Concentration: (Complexes)isQuasiIsomorphism_lpComplexMap_rp, =>
        ..., default value (-infinity,infinity),
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, True when the induced
        chain map toComplexMap phi is a quasi-isomorphism on the underlying
        complexes.

Description
===========

Computed by forwarding to isQuasiIsomorphism(toComplexMap phi) from the
Complexes package.  The underlying check inspects H_n of the induced chain map
at every degree in the concentration of the source and target.  The
Concentration option of the Complexes version is accepted and passed through.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z]                                                |
|                                                                    |
|o1 = R                                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                         |
|                                                                    |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                          |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                           |
|                               1,1   1,3                            |
|      Differential => {x, y, z}                                     |
|                                                                    |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : phi = identityDGAlgebraMap A                                   |
|                                                                    |
|o3 = map (R[T   ..T   ], R[T   ..T   ], {T   , T   , T   , x, y, z})|
|             1,1   1,3      1,1   1,3     1,1   1,2   1,3           |
|                                                                    |
|o3 : DGAlgebraMap                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isQuasiIsomorphism phi                                         |
|                                                                    |
|o4 = true                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

The identity DG algebra map is trivially a quasi-isomorphism.

