killCycles(DGModule) -- Adjoin free generators to kill the lowest nonvanishing homology of a DG module
******************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note killCycles: killCycles,
  * Usage: 
        Mnew = killCycles M
        Mnew = killCycles(M, StartDegree => s, EndDegree => e)
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A free DG module.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note StartDegree: killCycles_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStartDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 1, The smallest
        hom-degree at which to look for nontrivial homology. Defaults to 1.
      * *note EndDegree: killCycles_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value -1, The largest
        hom-degree at which to look; defaults to StartDegree (so by default a
        single degree is scanned).
      * *note Variable: killCycles_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null, Option to name the DG algebra generators
        adjoined by killCycles
  * Outputs:
      * Mnew, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, Either M
        itself (if homology vanishes throughout the requested range) or a free
        DG module with additional hom-degree n+1 generators, where n is the
        smallest degree in the range with H_n(M) != 0; the new generators'
        differentials are representative cycles of a minimal generating set for
        H_n(M).

Description
===========

The construction mirrors *note killCycles(DGAlgebra): killCycles, for DG
modules.  Scanning from StartDegree upwards, the method computes prune
homology(n, M) until it finds the first degree n with nontrivial homology.  It
then lifts the minimal homology generators provided by the pruning map back to
cycles in M_n and hands them to *note adjoinGenerators: adjoinGenerators,,
producing a new DG module in which those classes become boundaries.

A single call kills homology at one degree.  Iterating with successive
StartDegree values is how *note semifreeResolution: semifreeResolution, and
*note minimalSemifreeResolution: minimalSemifreeResolution, build resolutions.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x]                                            |
|                                                          |
|o1 = R                                                    |
|                                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                               |
|                                                          |
|o2 = {Ring => R                    }                      |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ]                       |
|                               1,1                        |
|      Differential => {x}                                 |
|                                                          |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0})                             |
|                                                          |
|o3 = {Base ring => R               }                      |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ]                               |
|                       1,1                                |
|                                 1                        |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ])                         |
|                            1,1                           |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}                       |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}                        |
|                                                          |
|o3 : DGModule                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : natGens = apply(rank M.natural, i -> (M.natural)_i)  |
|                                                          |
|o4 = {| 1 |}                                              |
|                                                          |
|o4 : List                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M2 = adjoinGenerators(M, {x * natGens#0})            |
|                                                          |
|o5 = {Base ring => R                       }              |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ]                               |
|                       1,1                                |
|                                 2                        |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ])                         |
|                            1,1                           |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 1}}               |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, | x |}                 |
|                                   | 0 |                  |
|                                                          |
|o5 : DGModule                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : prune homology(0, M2)                                |
|                                                          |
|o6 = cokernel | x |                                       |
|                                                          |
|                            1                             |
|o6 : R-module, quotient of R                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : M3 = killCycles(M2, StartDegree => 1, EndDegree => 2)|
|                                                          |
|o7 = {Base ring => R                                   }  |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ]                               |
|                       1,1                                |
|                                 3                        |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ])                         |
|                            1,1                           |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 1}}       |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, | x |, | -T_(1,1) |}   |
|                                   | 0 |  |     1    |    |
|                                   | 0 |  |     0    |    |
|                                                          |
|o7 : DGModule                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : prune homology(1, M3) == 0                           |
|                                                          |
|o8 = true                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

M2 has H_0 = R/(x) = k and no higher homology to kill, so M3 agrees with M2 in
this example. In settings where H_1 is nontrivial, killCycles adjoins one
hom-degree-2 generator per minimal H_1 class.

Caveat
======

Raises an error when StartDegree > EndDegree.  The input must be a free DG
module for the underlying homology computation to extract representative
cycles.

See also
========

  * *note Semifree resolutions of DG modules: Semifree resolutions of DG
    modules, -- Building semifree DG module resolutions via koszulComplexDGM,
    adjoinGenerators, killCycles, and semifreeResolution
  * *note adjoinGenerators: adjoinGenerators, -- Adjoin new free generators to
    a DG module with prescribed differentials
  * *note killCycles(DGAlgebra): killCycles, -- Adjoin variables to kill
    non-bounding cycles in the lowest positive degree
  * *note semifreeResolution: semifreeResolution, -- Build a semifree DG module
    resolving a module over the base ring
  * *note minimalSemifreeResolution: minimalSemifreeResolution, -- Build a
    minimal semifree DG module resolution over a DG algebra
  * *note StartDegree: StartDegree, -- Option to specify the first homological
    degree processed by an iterative DG construction
  * *note EndDegree: EndDegree, -- Option to specify the last homological
    degree processed by an iterative DG construction

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note killCycles(DGModule): killCycles_lpDGModule_rp, -- Adjoin free
    generators to kill the lowest nonvanishing homology of a DG module
