semifreeResolution -- Build a semifree DG module resolving a module over the base ring
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = semifreeResolution M
        F = semifreeResolution(A, M)
        F = semifreeResolution(A, M, EndDegree => n)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, A DG algebra
        over R = ring M.  If omitted, koszulComplexDGA(ring M) is used.
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, A module over A.ring.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note StartDegree: semifreeResolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStartDegree=>_pd_pd
        _pd_rp, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 1, First
        hom-degree at which to start killing homology.  Defaults to 1.
      * *note EndDegree: semifreeResolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 3, Last
        hom-degree at which to kill homology.  Defaults to 3.  Homology of F in
        the range [StartDegree, EndDegree] will vanish.
  * Outputs:
      * F, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A free DG module
        over A with H_0(F) = M and H_n(F) = 0 for StartDegree <= n <=
        EndDegree.

Description
===========

Starts from a free DG module with one hom-degree-0 generator per generator of
M, adjoins hom-degree-1 generators whose differentials are the columns of
presentation M lifted to A.natural (killing the presentation relations), and
then iterates *note killCycles(DGModule): killCycles_lpDGModule_rp, from
StartDegree through EndDegree.

This is the module-theoretic analog of *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, on
a DG algebra.  The output is a semifree DG module but is not guaranteed to be
minimal over A: relation columns are adjoined even when they are already
boundaries under the DG algebra differential.  For a minimal resolution, use
*note minimalSemifreeResolution: minimalSemifreeResolution,.

