minimalSemifreeResolution -- Build a minimal semifree DG module resolution over a DG algebra
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = minimalSemifreeResolution M
        F = minimalSemifreeResolution(A, M)
        F = minimalSemifreeResolution(A, M, EndDegree => n)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, A DG algebra
        over a (graded-)local ring R = ring M.  If omitted,
        koszulComplexDGA(ring M) is used.
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, A module over A.ring.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note StartDegree: minimalSemifreeResolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStartDegree
        =>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        1, First hom-degree at which to start killing homology.  Defaults to 1.
      * *note EndDegree: minimalSemifreeResolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd
        _pd_pd_rp, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 3,
        Last hom-degree at which to kill homology.  Defaults to 3.
  * Outputs:
      * F, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A semifree DG
        module resolving M over A, minimal in the sense that every generator's
        differential lands in the augmentation ideal of A.natural.

Description
===========

Produces a semifree resolution whose generator count in each hom-degree is
minimal among all semifree resolutions of M over A.  Two ingredients make the
output minimal:

First, M is replaced by prune M, giving a minimal presentation over the
(graded-)local base ring.  The number of hom-degree-0 generators is therefore
the minimal number of generators of M over R.

Second, each column of presentation(prune M) is tested with *note
getBoundaryPreimage: getBoundaryPreimage, against the DG-algebra-induced
differential.  If a relation is already a boundary, it is not adjoined; if only
a residue is a non-boundary, the adjoined generator's differential is that
residue rather than the original relation.  This is what makes the output
minimal over A, not merely over R.

The iterative *note killCycles(DGModule): killCycles_lpDGModule_rp, passes then
use the canonical pruning map of homology(n, F) to pick a minimal generating
set of representative cycles at each stage.

