Matrix factorizations on hypersurfaces.  Over a hypersurface R = Q/(f) every
maximal Cohen-Macaulay module's free resolution is eventually 2-periodic with
differentials forming a matrix factorization (phi, psi) of f (Eisenbud).  The
minimal semifree resolution over A = koszulComplexDGA(ideal f) exhibits this
periodicity directly in its printed differentials.  Here is the classic example
f = x^5:

