isMinimalSemifreeResolution -- Test whether a semifree DG module is minimal over its DG algebra
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isMinimalSemifreeResolution M
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, A free DG module
        (the intended use is on the output of *note semifreeResolution:
        semifreeResolution, or *note minimalSemifreeResolution:
        minimalSemifreeResolution,).
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true when each
        generator's differential lies in the augmentation ideal of A.natural,
        i.e. its reduction along A -> k (sending T_i -> 0 and then mod (vars
        R)) is zero.

Description
===========

Minimality over a DG algebra A means: after base change along the augmentation
A -> k, every differential of F becomes the zero map.  Equivalently, each
M.diff#i has all of its coefficients (in the free basis of M.natural) lying in
the augmentation ideal of A.natural generated by (vars R) and the
positive-hom-degree generators T_i.

This predicate checks only the structural minimality condition; it does not
verify acyclicity.  Use *note isAcyclic(DGModule): isAcyclic_lpDGModule_rp,
with an EndDegree option for that.

