subDGAlgebra -- The sub-DG algebra generated by a chosen subset of DG generators
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        B = subDGAlgebra(A, keepIdx)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * keepIdx, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of integers giving
        the indices (into 0 .. numgens A.natural - 1) of the DG generators to
        keep.  Duplicates and out-of-range indices raise an error.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * InitializeDegreeZeroHomology => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, Whether to compute H_0 of
        the result eagerly. Default true.
      * InitializeComplex => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, Whether to build the underlying complex eagerly.
        Default false.
  * Outputs:
      * B, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, A DG algebra
        over A.ring whose DG generators are the keepIdx-indexed generators of A
        in sorted order, with their differentials restricted accordingly.

Description
===========

The subset keepIdx must be d-closed: if the differential of a kept generator
uses a dropped generator, subDGAlgebra raises an error rather than silently
returning a non-DG object.  This protects downstream code from accidentally
producing inconsistent structures.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)       |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R               |
|                                          |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,2  |
|      Differential => {x, y}              |
|                                          |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = subDGAlgebra(A, {0})             |
|                                          |
|o3 = {Ring => R                    }      |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ]       |
|                               1,1        |
|      Differential => {x}                 |
|                                          |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : numgens B.natural                    |
|                                          |
|o4 = 1                                    |
+------------------------------------------+

Dropping a generator whose image is referenced in a kept generator's
differential is caught:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x] / ideal(x^2)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {Ring => R                    }                                         |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ]                                          |
|                               1,1                                           |
|      Differential => {x}                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : A' = adjoinVariables(A, {x * (gens A.natural)#0})                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {Ring => R                          }                                   |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   , T   ]                                    |
|                               1,1   2,1                                     |
|      Differential => {x, x*T   }                                            |
|                             1,1                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : try subDGAlgebra(A', {1}) else "error: kept differential uses dropped   |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = error: kept differential uses dropped generator                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|generator"                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Duplicate or out-of-range entries in keepIdx raise an error.  keepIdx is
internally sorted, so the generator order of the output depends only on which
indices appear.

