truncateGenerators -- Restrict a DG algebra to its generators of hom-degree strictly above a bound
**************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        B = truncateGenerators(A, n)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, A hom-degree bound; generators
        of hom-degree <= n are dropped.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * InitializeDegreeZeroHomology => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, Default true.
      * InitializeComplex => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, Default false.
  * Outputs:
      * B, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, The sub-DG
        algebra of A generated by the DG generators whose first-hom-degree
        component is strictly greater than n.

Description
===========

Computes keepIdx as select(0 .. #A.Degrees - 1, i -> first A.Degrees#i > n) and
delegates to *note subDGAlgebra: subDGAlgebra,.  As with *note subDGAlgebra:
subDGAlgebra,, the subset must be d-closed; if the differential of a generator
T_i of hom-degree > n uses a generator of hom-degree <= n that would be
dropped, an error is raised.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)       |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R               |
|                                          |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,2  |
|      Differential => {x, y}              |
|                                          |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = truncateGenerators(A, 0)         |
|                                          |
|o3 = {Ring => R                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,2  |
|      Differential => {x, y}              |
|                                          |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : numgens B.natural                    |
|                                          |
|o4 = 2                                    |
+------------------------------------------+

The Koszul algebra has all generators in hom-degree 1 so truncating below
degree 0 is a no-op in this case.

