===========

The semantic half of the well-definedness check: it verifies that the
differential squares to zero on every generator.  The structural half (*note
isValidDGAlgebra: isValidDGAlgebra,, and the corresponding isValidDGModule for
modules) is called first as a pre-condition.

This is the primitive called internally by *note isWellDefined(DGAlgebra):
isWellDefined_lpDGAlgebra_rp, and the user-facing *note
isWellDefined(DGModule): isWellDefined_lpDGModule_rp,.  It is exported for
low-level use when only the d^2 = 0 half of well-definedness needs to be
checked.

