Low-level differential computations and validity checks -- Primitives behind DG algebra and DG module differentials
*******************************************************************************************************************

The methods documented here implement the raw computations that higher-level DG
algebra and DG module routines rely on. They split into three groups.

The first group -- *note polyDifferential: polyDifferential, and *note
polyDiffMonomial: polyDiffMonomial, -- applies the Leibniz rule directly to
elements of A.natural to produce the DG algebra differential.
polyDifferential(n, A) returns the per-degree matrix A_n --> A_{n-1} over the
base ring and caches it inside A; polyDifferential(A, f) applies d to a single
element by summing over its terms; polyDiffMonomial(A, m) is the monomial
kernel that powers both.

The second group -- *note dgComplex: dgComplex, -- packages the per-degree
differentials of a DG algebra or DG module as a *note Complex:
(Complexes)Complex, of free modules over the base ring. The result is cached
and invalidated by *note invalidateDGAlgebraCache: invalidateDGAlgebraCache,.

The third group -- *note isValidDGModule: isValidDGModule, and *note
isDGSubmodule: isDGSubmodule, -- checks structural invariants. isValidDGModule
parallels *note isValidDGAlgebra: isValidDGAlgebra, and confirms that the
required keys are present with the expected types; isDGSubmodule tests whether
a given inclusion matrix has d-closed image without performing the d-saturation
that *note dgSubmodule: dgSubmodule, would.

Finally, *note getBoundaryPreimage: getBoundaryPreimage_lpDGModule_cmVector_rp,
lifts boundaries through the module differential, returning a preimage when one
exists and a residue otherwise.

See also
========

  * *note Basic operations on DG Algebras: Basic operations on DG Algebras, --
    Outlines some basic operations on DG Algebras
  * *note Building DG modules, submodules, and quotients: Building DG
    modules_cm submodules_cm and quotients, -- The DGModule / DGSubmodule /
    DGQuotientModule hierarchy and its constructors
  * *note Well-definedness, acyclicity, and quasi-isomorphism:
    Well-definedness_cm acyclicity_cm and quasi-isomorphism, -- Predicates that
    check DG-theoretic conditions on DG types
* Menu:

* polyDifferential::            Matrix and element-level differentials of a DG algebra
* polyDiffMonomial::            Leibniz rule on a single monomial of a DG algebra
* dgComplex::                   Package a DG algebra or DG module as a Complex of free base-ring modules
* isValidDGModule::             Structural-invariant check on a DG module
* isDGSubmodule::               Test whether the image of an inclusion matrix is d-closed
* getBoundaryPreimage(DGModule,Vector): getBoundaryPreimage_lpDGModule_cmVector_rp.  Lift a boundary in a DG module to a preimage under the differential
* getBoundaryPreimage(DGModule,List): getBoundaryPreimage_lpDGModule_cmList_rp.  Lift a list of boundaries sharing a hom-degree through the module differential
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

