dgComplex -- Package a DG algebra or DG module as a Complex of free base-ring modules
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = dgComplex A
        C = dgComplex M
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, A *note Complex:
        (Complexes)Complex, of free A.ring-modules whose i-th module is A_i
        (resp.\ M_i) and whose differential is polyDifferential (resp.\ *note
        moduleDifferential: moduleDifferential,).

Description
===========

dgComplex assembles the per-degree differentials of a DG algebra or DG module
into a single *note Complex: (Complexes)Complex, object.  The result is cached
on the input; calling dgComplex again returns exactly the same complex, and
*note invalidateDGAlgebraCache: invalidateDGAlgebraCache, clears the cache so
that the next call rebuilds the complex.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)         |
|                                            |
|o1 = R                                      |
|                                            |
|o1 : QuotientRing                           |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                 |
|                                            |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }  |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]   |
|                               1,1   1,2    |
|      Differential => {x, y}                |
|                                            |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                              |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C1 = dgComplex A                       |
|                                            |
|      1      2      1                       |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                        |
|                                            |
|     0      1      2                        |
|                                            |
|o3 : Complex                                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C2 = dgComplex A                       |
|                                            |
|      1      2      1                       |
|o4 = R  <-- R  <-- R                        |
|                                            |
|     0      1      2                        |
|                                            |
|o4 : Complex                                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(C1 === C2)                      |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : invalidateDGAlgebraCache A             |
|                                            |
|o6 = {Ring => R                          }  |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]   |
|                               1,1   1,2    |
|      Differential => {x, y}                |
|                                            |
|o6 : DGAlgebra                              |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(not A.cache#?(symbol dgComplex))|
+--------------------------------------------+
|i8 : C3 = dgComplex A                       |
|                                            |
|      1      2      1                       |
|o8 = R  <-- R  <-- R                        |
|                                            |
|     0      1      2                        |
|                                            |
|o8 : Complex                                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(instance(C3, Complex))          |
+--------------------------------------------+

When maxDegree is infinite -- for example on the acyclic closure of a
non-regular ring -- dgComplex truncates at a canonical finite bound so that a
*note Complex: (Complexes)Complex, is always produced.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i10 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)          |
|                                              |
|o10 = R                                       |
|                                              |
|o10 : QuotientRing                            |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i11 : A = acyclicClosure(R, EndDegree => 2)   |
|                                              |
|o11 = {Ring => R                             }|
|       Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]    |
|                                1,1   2,2     |
|       Differential => {x, y, x*T   , y*T   } |
|                                 1,1     1,2  |
|                                              |
|o11 : DGAlgebra                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i12 : assert(instance(dgComplex A, Complex))  |
+----------------------------------------------+

The DG module form is parallel: it builds the complex whose terms are M_i and
whose differentials are the maps returned by *note moduleDifferential:
moduleDifferential,.

+------------------------------------------+
|i13 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)      |
|                                          |
|o13 = R                                   |
|                                          |
|o13 : QuotientRing                        |
+------------------------------------------+
|i14 : KM = koszulComplexDGM R^1           |
|                                          |
|o14 = {Base ring => R                    }|
|       DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]        |
|                        1,1   1,2         |
|                                        1 |
|       Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])  |
|                             1,1   1,2    |
|       Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}      |
|       Differentials on gens => {0}       |
|                                          |
|o14 : DGModule                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i15 : D1 = dgComplex KM                   |
|                                          |
|       1      2      1                    |
|o15 = R  <-- R  <-- R                     |
|                                          |
|      0      1      2                     |
|                                          |
|o15 : Complex                             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i16 : D2 = dgComplex KM                   |
|                                          |
|       1      2      1                    |
|o16 = R  <-- R  <-- R                     |
|                                          |
|      0      1      2                     |
|                                          |
|o16 : Complex                             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i17 : assert(D1 === D2)                   |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Low-level differential computations and validity checks: Low-level
    differential computations and validity checks, -- Primitives behind DG
    algebra and DG module differentials
  * *note polyDifferential: polyDifferential, -- Matrix and element-level
    differentials of a DG algebra
  * *note moduleDifferential: moduleDifferential, -- The hom-degree-n
    differential of a DG module as a matrix over the base ring
  * *note invalidateDGAlgebraCache: invalidateDGAlgebraCache, -- Discard cached
    derived data so that it is recomputed from scratch
  * *note toComplex: toComplex, -- Converts a DGAlgebra to a Complex

Ways to use dgComplex:
======================

  * "dgComplex(DGAlgebra)"
  * "dgComplex(DGModule)"

