isValidDGModule -- Structural-invariant check on a DG module
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isValidDGModule M
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if the stored
        DGModule has all required keys with the expected types; false
        otherwise.

Description
===========

isValidDGModule parallels *note isValidDGAlgebra: isValidDGAlgebra,: it
confirms that M carries the keys dgAlgebra, ring, natural, Degrees, and diff
with the expected types, that the referenced DGAlgebra is itself structurally
valid, and that the generator-degree list has the same length as the
differential list.  It does not verify the semantic property d_M^2 = 0; that is
the job of *note isWellDefinedDifferential: isWellDefinedDifferential,, and the
two together are what the user-facing *note isWellDefined(DGModule):
isWellDefined_lpDGModule_rp, calls.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)      |
|                                         |
|o1 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : QuotientRing                        |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : KM = koszulComplexDGM R^1           |
|                                         |
|o2 = {Base ring => R                    }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]        |
|                       1,1   1,2         |
|                                       1 |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])  |
|                            1,1   1,2    |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}      |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}       |
|                                         |
|o2 : DGModule                            |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert(isValidDGModule KM)          |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Low-level differential computations and validity checks: Low-level
    differential computations and validity checks, -- Primitives behind DG
    algebra and DG module differentials
  * *note Well-definedness, acyclicity, and quasi-isomorphism:
    Well-definedness_cm acyclicity_cm and quasi-isomorphism, -- Predicates that
    check DG-theoretic conditions on DG types
  * *note isValidDGAlgebra: isValidDGAlgebra, -- Structural invariant check for
    a DG algebra
  * *note isWellDefinedDifferential: isWellDefinedDifferential, -- Semantic
    check that d^2 = 0 for a DG algebra or DG module
  * *note isWellDefined(DGModule): isWellDefined_lpDGModule_rp, -- Check that a
    DG module has correct structure and that its differential squares to zero

Ways to use isValidDGModule:
============================

  * "isValidDGModule(DGModule)"

