Accessors and cache management -- Reading state out of a DG algebra or DG module and maintaining its caches
***********************************************************************************************************

A *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra, or *note DGModule: DGModule, stores its defining
data in a small collection of keys -- the base ring, the graded-commutative
algebra, the generator degrees, and the list of generator differentials --
together with a cache of derived information (per-degree differential matrices,
homology, the homology algebra, a *note Complex: (Complexes)Complex,
presentation).  This page collects the two groups of utilities that manage that
state.

The first group -- *note underlyingRing: underlyingRing,, *note
underlyingAlgebra: underlyingAlgebra,, *note differential: differential,, and
*note generatorDegrees: generatorDegrees, -- returns the four defining
ingredients.  Because both DG algebras and DG modules carry the same names,
code can remain agnostic about which one it is handling.

The second group -- *note ensureDGAlgebraCaches: ensureDGAlgebraCaches, and
*note invalidateDGAlgebraCache: invalidateDGAlgebraCache, -- maintains the
cache sub-tables.  ensureDGAlgebraCaches is idempotent and guarantees that the
standard cache keys are present with the expected types; *note
invalidateDGAlgebraCache: invalidateDGAlgebraCache, wipes every cached computed
value so that the next call recomputes from scratch.  Routines such as *note
setDiff: setDiff, that mutate the differential call *note
invalidateDGAlgebraCache: invalidateDGAlgebraCache, internally so that stale
homology and stale differential matrices are never served.

See also
========

  * *note Basic operations on DG Algebras: Basic operations on DG Algebras, --
    Outlines some basic operations on DG Algebras
  * *note Building DG modules, submodules, and quotients: Building DG
    modules_cm submodules_cm and quotients, -- The DGModule / DGSubmodule /
    DGQuotientModule hierarchy and its constructors
  * *note Low-level differential computations and validity checks: Low-level
    differential computations and validity checks, -- Primitives behind DG
    algebra and DG module differentials
* Menu:

* underlyingRing::              The commutative base ring of a DG algebra or DG module
* underlyingAlgebra::           The graded-commutative algebra carrying the DG structure
* differential::                The list of generator differentials stored in a DG algebra or DG module
* generatorDegrees::            The hom-degrees (and optional internal degrees) of the DG generators
* ensureDGAlgebraCaches::       Guarantee that the standard cache sub-tables are present
* invalidateDGAlgebraCache::    Discard cached derived data so that it is recomputed from scratch
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in DGAlgebras/doc.m2:7253:0.

