underlyingRing -- The commutative base ring of a DG algebra or DG module
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = underlyingRing A
        S = underlyingRing M
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, The commutative base ring A.ring
        or M.ring over which the DG structure is defined.

Description
===========

underlyingRing returns the base ring.  This is the ring R in the DG algebra A =
R\langle T_1, T_2, \ldots \rangle or the DG module M, and it is the ring over
which every matrix returned by *note polyDifferential: polyDifferential, or
*note moduleDifferential: moduleDifferential, is built.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)       |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R               |
|                                          |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,2  |
|      Differential => {x, y}              |
|                                          |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert(underlyingRing A === R)       |
+------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = koszulComplexDGM R^1            |
|                                         |
|o4 = {Base ring => R                    }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]        |
|                       1,1   1,2         |
|                                       1 |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])  |
|                            1,1   1,2    |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}      |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}       |
|                                         |
|o4 : DGModule                            |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(underlyingRing M === R)      |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Accessors and cache management: Accessors and cache management, --
    Reading state out of a DG algebra or DG module and maintaining its caches
  * *note underlyingAlgebra: underlyingAlgebra, -- The graded-commutative
    algebra carrying the DG structure
  * *note differential: differential, -- The list of generator differentials
    stored in a DG algebra or DG module
  * *note generatorDegrees: generatorDegrees, -- The hom-degrees (and optional
    internal degrees) of the DG generators

Ways to use underlyingRing:
===========================

  * "underlyingRing(DGAlgebra)"
  * "underlyingRing(DGModule)"

