underlyingAlgebra -- The graded-commutative algebra carrying the DG structure
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = underlyingAlgebra A
        N = underlyingAlgebra M
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, The graded-commutative ring
        A.natural (the DG algebra's own ring) or, for a DG module, the graded
        free module M.natural (as a *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, over
        A.natural).

Description
===========

For a *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, underlyingAlgebra returns the
graded-commutative ring A.natural -- the ring whose elements one manipulates
when writing polynomials in the DG generators.  For a *note DGModule: DGModule,
it returns the underlying A.natural-module M.natural on which the differential
acts.  In both cases the result is what you typically use before referring to
DG generators by name.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)           |
|                                              |
|o1 = R                                        |
|                                              |
|o1 : QuotientRing                             |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                   |
|                                              |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }    |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]     |
|                               1,1   1,2      |
|      Differential => {x, y}                  |
|                                              |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert(underlyingAlgebra A === A.natural)|
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : numgens underlyingAlgebra A              |
|                                              |
|o4 = 2                                        |
+----------------------------------------------+
+----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M = koszulComplexDGM R^1                 |
|                                              |
|o5 = {Base ring => R                    }     |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]             |
|                       1,1   1,2              |
|                                       1      |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])       |
|                            1,1   1,2         |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}           |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}            |
|                                              |
|o5 : DGModule                                 |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(underlyingAlgebra M === M.natural)|
+----------------------------------------------+

