DG module primitives and chain-complex export -- Installing differentials, reading degree data, and exporting to Complex
************************************************************************************************************************

This page collects the remaining DG module primitives (installing a
differential, asking for the largest hom-degree, reading off a per-degree
basis) together with the methods that export a DG algebra, DG module, DG module
map, or DG ideal to the ordinary *note Complex: (Complexes)Complex, / *note
ComplexMap: (Complexes)ComplexMap, world.

Installing a differential.  *note setDiff(DGModule,List):
setDiff_lpDGModule_cmList_rp, is the DG module analogue of *note
setDiff(DGAlgebra,List): setDiff,: it records the image of each natural
generator under d_M and invalidates every cached derived value.

Reading degree data.  *note maxDegree(DGModule): maxDegree_lpDGModule_rp, and
*note maxDegree(DGQuotientModule): maxDegree_lpDGQuotientModule_rp, report the
largest hom-degree present (or infinity if the underlying DG algebra has an
even-degree generator). *note getBasis(ZZ,DGModule):
getBasis_lpZZ_cmDGModule_rp, returns an A.ring-basis of the hom-degree-n piece
of M.natural.

Exporting to *note Complex: (Complexes)Complex,.  The *note toComplex:
toComplex, family packages per-degree differentials as a plain *note Complex:
(Complexes)Complex, of free base-ring modules; the *note toComplexMap:
toComplexMap, family packages per-degree induced maps as a *note ComplexMap:
(Complexes)ComplexMap,.  Together they let the chain-level results of the DG
machinery be handed off to the rest of the *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top,
package.

Block-diagonal display.  *note displayBlockDiff: displayBlockDiff, prints the
per-internal-multidegree block decomposition of a DG algebra differential at a
given homological degree, convenient for inspecting the acyclic closure of a
multigraded quotient.

See also
========

  * *note Basic operations on DG Algebras: Basic operations on DG Algebras, --
    Outlines some basic operations on DG Algebras
  * *note Building DG modules, submodules, and quotients: Building DG
    modules_cm submodules_cm and quotients, -- The DGModule / DGSubmodule /
    DGQuotientModule hierarchy and its constructors
  * *note Low-level differential computations and validity checks: Low-level
    differential computations and validity checks, -- Primitives behind DG
    algebra and DG module differentials
* Menu:

* setDiff(DGModule,List): setDiff_lpDGModule_cmList_rp.  Install the list of generator differentials on a free DG module
* maxDegree(DGModule): maxDegree_lpDGModule_rp.  Largest hom-degree present in a DG module
* maxDegree(DGQuotientModule): maxDegree_lpDGQuotientModule_rp.  Largest hom-degree present in a DG quotient module
* getBasis(ZZ,DGModule): getBasis_lpZZ_cmDGModule_rp.  Basis of the hom-degree-n piece of a DG module
* toComplex(DGModule): toComplex_lpDGModule_rp.  Export a DG module to a Complex of free base-ring modules
* toComplex(DGModule,ZZ): toComplex_lpDGModule_cmZZ_rp.  Export a DG module to a Complex with an explicit hom-degree bound
* toComplex(DGQuotientModule): toComplex_lpDGQuotientModule_rp.  Export a DG quotient module to a Complex
* toComplex(DGIdeal): toComplex_lpDGIdeal_rp.  Export a DG ideal to a Complex (not yet implemented)
* toComplexMap(DGModuleMap): toComplexMap_lpDGModuleMap_rp.  Export a DG module map to a ComplexMap
* toComplexMap(DGModuleMap,ZZ): toComplexMap_lpDGModuleMap_cmZZ_rp.  The per-hom-degree component of a DG module map as a matrix
* displayBlockDiff::            Shows natural decomposition of a map in the Tate resolution
