maxDegree(DGQuotientModule) -- Largest hom-degree present in a DG quotient module
*********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note maxDegree: maxDegree,
  * Usage: 
        n = maxDegree Q
  * Inputs:
      * Q, an instance of the type *note DGQuotientModule: DGQuotientModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or an *note infinite number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)InfiniteNumber,, The maxDegree of the ambient DG module
        Q.ambient.

Description
===========

Passing a DG quotient module to *note maxDegree: maxDegree, returns the max
hom-degree of its ambient DG module.  Because taking a quotient cannot
introduce elements of higher hom-degree than are already in the ambient, the
ambient's bound is valid for the quotient.  The value is what *note
toComplex(DGQuotientModule): toComplex_lpDGQuotientModule_rp, and *note
toComplexMap(DGModuleMap): toComplexMap_lpDGModuleMap_rp, use to decide where
to truncate when no *note EndDegree: EndDegree, is supplied.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x]                          |
|                                            |
|o1 = R                                      |
|                                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                         |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                 |
|                                            |
|o2 = {Ring => R                    }        |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ]         |
|                               1,1          |
|      Differential => {x}                   |
|                                            |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                              |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = freeDGModule(A, {0, 1})            |
|                                            |
|o3 = {Base ring => R                       }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ]                 |
|                       1,1                  |
|                                 2          |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ])           |
|                            1,1             |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}, {1, 0}} |
|      Differentials on gens => {0, 0}       |
|                                            |
|o3 : DGModule                               |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : z = zeroDGModuleMap(M, M)              |
|                                            |
|                         2                  |
|o4 = {Source => (R[T   ]) }                 |
|                    1,1                     |
|                         2                  |
|      Target => (R[T   ])                   |
|                    1,1                     |
|      Natural => 0                          |
|                                            |
|o4 : DGModuleMap                            |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Q = cokernel z                         |
|                                            |
|o5 = DGQuotientModule Q = M / S             |
|                          2                 |
|     Q.natural = (R[T   ])                  |
|                     1,1                    |
|     Degrees   = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}}           |
|                                            |
|o5 : DGQuotientModule                       |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(maxDegree Q == maxDegree M)     |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note DG module primitives and chain-complex export: DG module primitives
    and chain-complex export, -- Installing differentials, reading degree data,
    and exporting to Complex
  * *note maxDegree: maxDegree, -- Computes the maximum homological degree of a
    DGAlgebra
  * *note maxDegree(DGModule): maxDegree_lpDGModule_rp, -- Largest hom-degree
    present in a DG module
  * *note toComplex(DGQuotientModule): toComplex_lpDGQuotientModule_rp, --
    Export a DG quotient module to a Complex

