getBasis(ZZ,DGModule) -- Basis of the hom-degree-n piece of a DG module
***********************************************************************

  * Function: *note getBasis: getBasis,
  * Usage: 
        b = getBasis(n, M)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, A homological degree.
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Limit: getBasis_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value -1, Maximum number of basis elements to return from
        getBasis
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, A one-row matrix over
        M.natural whose entries are the basis elements of F_n(M), the
        hom-degree-n piece of M.natural over A.ring.

Description
===========

getBasis(n, M) delegates to *note basis: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, on the underlying
A.natural-module M.natural, restricting to the variables of A.natural.  The
result is the piece of M on which moduleDifferential(n, M) acts as its
source-side basis.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)              |
|                                                 |
|o1 = R                                           |
|                                                 |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : KM = koszulComplexDGM R^1                   |
|                                                 |
|o2 = {Base ring => R                    }        |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                |
|                       1,1   1,2                 |
|                                       1         |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])          |
|                            1,1   1,2            |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}              |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}               |
|                                                 |
|o2 : DGModule                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : b = getBasis(1, KM)                         |
|                                                 |
|o3 = | T_(1,1) T_(1,2) |                         |
|                                                 |
|                           1                    2|
|o3 : Matrix (R[T   ..T   ])  <-- (R[T   ..T   ]) |
|                1,1   1,2            1,1   1,2   |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert(instance(b, Matrix))                 |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(numcols b == 2)                      |
+-------------------------------------------------+

