toComplex(DGModule) -- Export a DG module to a Complex of free base-ring modules
********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note toComplex: toComplex,
  * Usage: 
        C = toComplex M
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, A *note Complex:
        (Complexes)Complex, of free A.ring-modules whose i-th differential is
        moduleDifferential(i+1, M).

Description
===========

toComplex packages the per-degree module differentials as an ordinary *note
Complex: (Complexes)Complex, so that the result can flow through the rest of
the *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top, package.  The one-argument form uses
maxDegree M as the truncation bound and errors out if that is infinity; use
*note toComplex(DGModule,ZZ): toComplex_lpDGModule_cmZZ_rp, to supply an
explicit bound. The result is not cached by this method (use *note dgComplex:
dgComplex, for a cached variant).

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y] / ideal(x^2, y^2)             |
|                                                |
|o1 = R                                          |
|                                                |
|o1 : QuotientRing                               |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : KM = koszulComplexDGM R^1                  |
|                                                |
|o2 = {Base ring => R                    }       |
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]               |
|                       1,1   1,2                |
|                                       1        |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])         |
|                            1,1   1,2           |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}             |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}              |
|                                                |
|o2 : DGModule                                   |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = toComplex KM                           |
|                                                |
|      1      2      1                           |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                            |
|                                                |
|     0      1      2                            |
|                                                |
|o3 : Complex                                    |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert(instance(C, Complex))               |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(C.dd_1 == moduleDifferential(1, KM))|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(C.dd_2 == moduleDifferential(2, KM))|
+------------------------------------------------+

