toComplex(DGModule,ZZ) -- Export a DG module to a Complex with an explicit hom-degree bound
*******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note toComplex: toComplex,
  * Usage: 
        C = toComplex(M, n)
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note DGModule: DGModule,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, A hom-degree upper bound.
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, A *note Complex:
        (Complexes)Complex, of free A.ring-modules, truncated at hom-degree n.

Description
===========

The explicit-bound form of *note toComplex(DGModule): toComplex_lpDGModule_rp,.
Supplying a bound is required when the ambient DG algebra has infinite
hom-degree (as for an *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure,), and convenient
when a low bound suffices.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x, y, z]                     |
|                                         |
|o1 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : KM = koszulComplexDGM R^1           |
|                                         |
|o2 = {Base ring => R                    }|
|      DG algebra => R[T   ..T   ]        |
|                       1,1   1,3         |
|                                       1 |
|      Natural module => (R[T   ..T   ])  |
|                            1,1   1,3    |
|      Generator degrees => {{0, 0}}      |
|      Differentials on gens => {0}       |
|                                         |
|o2 : DGModule                            |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = toComplex(KM, 2)                |
|                                         |
|      1      3      3                    |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                     |
|                                         |
|     0      1      2                     |
|                                         |
|o3 : Complex                             |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert(instance(C, Complex))        |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(max C == 2)                  |
+-----------------------------------------+

