toComplexMap(DGModuleMap) -- Export a DG module map to a ComplexMap
*******************************************************************

  * Function: *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap,
  * Usage: 
        cm = toComplexMap f
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note DGModuleMap: DGModuleMap,, A DG module
        map M --> N.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AssertWellDefined: toComplexMap, => ..., default value true,
        Construct the ComplexMap associated to a DGAlgebraMap
      * *note EndDegree: toComplexMap, => ..., default value -1, Construct the
        ComplexMap associated to a DGAlgebraMap
  * Outputs:
      * cm, a *note map of complexes: (Complexes)ComplexMap,, The induced *note
        ComplexMap: (Complexes)ComplexMap, toComplex M --> toComplex N.

Description
===========

toComplexMap f assembles the per-degree pieces of f into a *note ComplexMap:
(Complexes)ComplexMap,.  When either side has infinite hom-degree, an *note
EndDegree: EndDegree, bound must be supplied; the option *note
AssertWellDefined: AssertWellDefined, (default true) causes isWellDefined f to
be checked up front.  When the target is a DG quotient module only the
canonical projection is supported; the result is the induced quotient chain
map.  Use *note toComplexMap(DGModuleMap,ZZ):
toComplexMap_lpDGModuleMap_cmZZ_rp, to extract a single per-degree component
instead.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a, b] / ideal(a^2, b^2)                        |
|                                                           |
|o1 = R                                                     |
|                                                           |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                |
|                                                           |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                 |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                  |
|                               1,1   1,2                   |
|      Differential => {a, b}                               |
|                                                           |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : phi = dgAlgebraMap(A, A, matrix {gens A.natural})     |
|                                                           |
|o3 = map (R[T   ..T   ], R[T   ..T   ], {T   , T   , a, b})|
|             1,1   1,2      1,1   1,2     1,1   1,2        |
|                                                           |
|o3 : DGAlgebraMap                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : cm = toComplexMap phi                                 |
|                                                           |
|          1             1                                  |
|o4 = 0 : R  <--------- R  : 0                              |
|               | 1 |                                       |
|                                                           |
|          2                   2                            |
|     1 : R  <--------------- R  : 1                        |
|               {1} | 1 0 |                                 |
|               {1} | 0 1 |                                 |
|                                                           |
|          1                 1                              |
|     2 : R  <------------- R  : 2                          |
|               {2} | 1 |                                   |
|                                                           |
|o4 : ComplexMap                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(instance(cm, ComplexMap))                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

