acyclicClosure(...,EndDegree=>...) -- Option to specify the degree to stop computing the acyclic closure
********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        A =  acyclicClosure(B,EndDegree=>n)
  * Inputs:
      * B, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

All generators of the acyclic closure will be found up to homological degree n.
Note that B can be an ordinary ring, a factor ring of a polynomial ring,
treated as a DGAlgebra generated in homological degree 0, as in the following
example:

The default value of EndDegree is 3.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z,w]/(ideal"x3,y3,z3,x2yz")                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : acyclicClosure R                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {Ring => R                                                              |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ..T   , T   ..T   ]            |
|                               1,1   2,4   3,1   3,3   4,1   4,6             |
