AssertWellDefined -- Option to verify that a constructed DG algebra map respects differentials
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        liftToDGMap(..., AssertWellDefined => true)
        toComplexMap(..., AssertWellDefined => true)

Description
===========

When set to true, the constructor checks that the output *note DGAlgebraMap:
DGAlgebraMap, or the resulting *note ComplexMap: (Complexes)ComplexMap,
actually commutes with the differentials up to the working degree.  This is a
false by default because the check can be expensive for large acyclic closures;
set it to true when debugging a DG map that behaves unexpectedly.

See also
========

  * *note liftToDGMap: liftToDGMap, -- Lift a ring homomorphism in degree zero
    to a DG algebra morphism
  * *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap, -- Construct the ComplexMap associated to
    a DGAlgebraMap
  * *note dgAlgebraMap: dgAlgebraMap, -- Define a DG algebra map between DG
    algebras.

Functions with optional argument named AssertWellDefined:
=========================================================

  * "toComplexMap(...,AssertWellDefined=>...)" -- see *note toComplexMap:
    toComplexMap, -- Construct the ComplexMap associated to a DGAlgebraMap

