cycles -- Chosen cycle representatives for homology generators of a DG algebra
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        A.cycles

Description
===========

When *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure,, *note killCycles: killCycles,, or
*note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, adjoin new generators to kill homology
of a DG algebra A, the chosen cycle representatives are cached on the output so
the exact Tate construction can be inspected afterwards.  The key is A.cycles
on a DG algebra, or HA.cache.cycles on the output of *note homologyAlgebra:
homologyAlgebra,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a, b, c, d] / ideal(a^3, b^4, c^5, d^6)                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                                   |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                                    |
|                               1,1   1,4                                     |
|      Differential => {a, b, c, d}                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : apply(maxDegree A + 1, i -> numgens prune homology(i, A))               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {1, 4, 6, 4, 1}                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : HA = homologyAlgebra A                                                  |
|Finding easy relations           :  -- used 0.0264601s (cpu); 0.0236543s     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = HA                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)                          |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|(thread); 0s (gc)                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : numgens HA                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 4                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : HA.cache.cycles                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|       2       3       4       5                                             |
|o6 = {a T   , b T   , c T   , d T   }                                        |
|         1,1     1,2     1,3     1,4                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The entries of HA.cache.cycles are elements of A.natural: cycles chosen to
represent the generators of HA as an algebra.  These are the same
representatives that would be used as the differentials of newly adjoined
generators in *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure,.

See also
========

  * *note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, -- Compute the homology algebra of
    a DGAlgebra.
  * *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, -- Tate's construction of a semifree
    acyclic DG algebra extension
  * *note killCycles: killCycles, -- Adjoin variables to kill non-bounding
    cycles in the lowest positive degree

For the programmer
==================

The object *note cycles: cycles, is a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

