dgAlgebraMap -- Define a DG algebra map between DG algebras.
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        phi = dgAlgebraMap(B,A,M)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, Source
      * B, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, Target
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, A matrix representing where
        the generators of A should be mapped to (akin to ringMap)
  * Outputs:
      * phi, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap,, 

Description
===========

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c]/ideal{a^3+b^3+c^3,a*b*c}               |
|                                                              |
|o1 = R                                                        |
|                                                              |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : K1 = koszulComplexDGA(ideal vars R,Variable=>"Y")        |
|                                                              |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                    |
|      Underlying algebra => R[Y   ..Y   ]                     |
|                               1,1   1,3                      |
|      Differential => {a, b, c}                               |
|                                                              |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : K2 = koszulComplexDGA(ideal {b,c},Variable=>"T")         |
|                                                              |
|o3 = {Ring => R                          }                    |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                     |
|                               1,1   1,2                      |
|      Differential => {b, c}                                  |
|                                                              |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = dgAlgebraMap(K1,K2,matrix{{Y_(1,2),Y_(1,3)}})        |
|                                                              |
|o4 = map (R[Y   ..Y   ], R[T   ..T   ], {Y   , Y   , a, b, c})|
|             1,1   1,3      1,1   1,2     1,2   1,3           |
|                                                              |
|o4 : DGAlgebraMap                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isWellDefined g                                          |
|                                                              |
|o5 = true                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

The function does not check that the DG algebra map is well defined, however.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f = dgAlgebraMap(K2,K1,matrix{{0,T_(1,1),T_(1,2)}})         |
|                                                                 |
|o6 = map (R[T   ..T   ], R[Y   ..Y   ], {0, T   , T   , a, b, c})|
|             1,1   1,2      1,1   1,3        1,1   1,2           |
|                                                                 |
|o6 : DGAlgebraMap                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined f                                             |
|                                                                 |
|o7 = false                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

