diff(DGAlgebra,RingElement) -- Apply the differential of a DGAlgebra to a ring element
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note diff: (Macaulay2Doc)diff,
  * Usage: 
        b = diff(A, a)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * a, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of
        A.natural
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the image d_A(a)

Description
===========

Returns the image of a under the differential of A. The element a must be a
ring element of the underlying graded-commutative algebra A.natural; products,
sums, and polynomial expressions in the DG generators are all valid inputs.
The differential is applied by the Leibniz rule, so homogeneous components are
processed independently.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z]                            |
|                                                  |
|o1 = R                                            |
|                                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                       |
|                                                  |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }        |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]         |
|                               1,1   1,3          |
|      Differential => {x, y, z}                   |
|                                                  |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : diff(A, T_(1,1) * T_(1,2))                   |
|                                                  |
|o3 = - y*T    + x*T                               |
|          1,1      1,2                            |
|                                                  |
|o3 : R[T   ..T   ]                                |
|        1,1   1,3                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : diff(A, diff(A, T_(1,1) * T_(1,2) * T_(1,3)))|
|                                                  |
|o4 = 0                                            |
|                                                  |
|o4 : R[T   ..T   ]                                |
|        1,1   1,3                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------+

When a is a cycle, the result is zero:

+------------------------------+
|i5 : z = x*T_(1,2) - y*T_(1,1)|
|                              |
|o5 = - y*T    + x*T           |
|          1,1      1,2        |
|                              |
|o5 : R[T   ..T   ]            |
|        1,1   1,3             |
+------------------------------+
|i6 : diff(A, z)               |
|                              |
|o6 = 0                        |
|                              |
|o6 : R[T   ..T   ]            |
|        1,1   1,3             |
+------------------------------+

To solve the equation diff(A, b) == z for a boundary z, use *note
getBoundaryPreimage: getBoundaryPreimage,.

See also
========

  * *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra, -- The class of all DGAlgebras
  * *note getBoundaryPreimage: getBoundaryPreimage, -- Attempt to find a
    preimage of a boundary under the differential of a DGAlgebra.
  * *note homologyClass: homologyClass, -- Computes the element of the homology
    algebra corresponding to a cycle in a DGAlgebra.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note diff(DGAlgebra,RingElement): diff_lpDGAlgebra_cmRingElement_rp, --
    Apply the differential of a DGAlgebra to a ring element
