EndDegree -- Option to specify the last homological degree processed by an iterative DG construction
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        acyclicClosure(..., EndDegree => n)
        killCycles(..., EndDegree => n)
        isAcyclic(..., EndDegree => n)
        toComplexMap(..., EndDegree => n)

Description
===========

Bounds how far an iterative DG algebra computation should proceed.  In *note
acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, this limits the homological degree of new
generators adjoined; in *note isAcyclic: isAcyclic, it is the highest degree in
which homology is checked; in *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap, it governs how
many homological degrees of the resulting chain map are computed.

The default value varies by function and is documented on each specific
bracketed option node.  This option is required whenever a DG algebra has
generators in even homological degree, since the algebra is otherwise
unbounded.

See also
========

  * *note StartDegree: StartDegree, -- Option to specify the first homological
    degree processed by an iterative DG construction
  * *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, -- Tate's construction of a semifree
    acyclic DG algebra extension
  * *note killCycles: killCycles, -- Adjoin variables to kill non-bounding
    cycles in the lowest positive degree
  * *note isAcyclic: isAcyclic, -- Determine whether a DG algebra has no higher
    homology
  * *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap, -- Construct the ComplexMap associated to
    a DGAlgebraMap

Functions with optional argument named EndDegree:
=================================================

  * *note acyclicClosure(...,EndDegree=>...):
    acyclicClosure_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- Option to specify
    the degree to stop computing the acyclic closure
  * *note isAcyclic(...,EndDegree=>...):
    isAcyclic_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- Option to specify the
