freeDGAlgebra -- Construct a free DG algebra with given generator degrees
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        A = freeDGAlgebra(R, degreeList)
        A = freeDGAlgebra(R, degreeList, Variable => "U")
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, The base ring over which the DG
        algebra is defined.
      * degreeList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, One degree per algebra
        generator.  Each degree is itself a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of
        integers; the first entry is interpreted as the homological degree, and
        any remaining entries are internal gradings carried through to the
        underlying algebra.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Variable => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "T",
        Either a base name (*note String: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or *note
        Symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,) or an explicit list of symbols.
        Defaults to "T".  See below.
  * Outputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, A DG algebra
        over R whose A.natural is a graded-commutative polynomial ring on
        #degreeList generators.  The differential is not set by this
        constructor; call *note setDiff: setDiff, on the result to install it.

Description
===========

The output is a *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra, whose underlying ring is a
polynomial ring in graded-commutative generators: generators of odd homological
degree are skew-commutative and square to zero (i.e.\ exterior), while
generators of even homological degree are fully commutative.  The resulting
algebra is always free as a graded R-algebra; the current version of the
package does not handle quotient DG algebras whose underlying ring is a
non-polynomial quotient.

Variable-naming convention.  Generators are named base_(i, j), where i is the
homological degree (the first entry of the degree vector) and j is a 1-indexed
counter among generators at that hom-degree. So freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {1},
{1}, {3}}) produces four generators T_(1,1), T_(1,2), T_(1,3), T_(3,1).  The
Variable option changes the base name:

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y, z]                                        |
|                                                                |
|o1 = R                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {1}, {1}, {3}}, Variable => "U")|
|                                                                |
|o2 = {Ring => R                                }                |
|      Underlying algebra => R[U   ..U   , U   ]                 |
|                               1,1   1,3   3,1                  |
|      Differential => null                                      |
|                                                                |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : gens A.natural                                             |
|                                                                |
|o3 = {U   , U   , U   , U   }                                   |
|       1,1   1,2   1,3   3,1                                    |
|                                                                |
|o3 : List                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

Passing a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of symbols for Variable overrides the
doubly-indexed naming entirely and uses the given names verbatim.  The list
length must match #degreeList:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {1}, {1}}, Variable => {getSymbol "P",       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {Ring => R                        }                                     |
|      Underlying algebra => R[P..Q, RR]                                      |
|      Differential => null                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|getSymbol "Q", getSymbol "RR"})                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : gens B.natural                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {P, Q, RR}                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This is the mode used internally by *note adjoinVariables: adjoinVariables, and
*note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, to preserve the identities of existing
generators when extending a DG algebra.

Multi-grading.  Any degree entries beyond the first are carried through as
additional gradings of the underlying ring A.natural.  To make the differential
homogeneous with respect to both the homological and internal gradings, pair
each hom-degree with the matching internal-degree of its image under *note
setDiff: setDiff,.  Here, T_(1,i) has degree (1,1) (hom-degree 1,
internal-degree 1) matching x, y, z, and T_(3,1) has degree (3,3) matching its
cubic-monomial differential:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Bmulti = freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1, 1}, {1, 1}, {1, 1}, {3, 3}})             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {Ring => R                                }                             |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                              |
|                               1,1   1,3   3,1                               |
|      Differential => null                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : degrees Bmulti.natural                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {{1, 1}, {1, 1}, {1, 1}, {3, 3}}                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : setDiff(Bmulti, {x, y, z, x*T_(1,2)*T_(1,3) - y*T_(1,1)*T_(1,3) +       |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = {Ring => R                                                      }       |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                              |
|                               1,1   1,3   3,1                               |
|      Differential => {x, y, z, z*T   T    - y*T   T    + x*T   T   }        |
|                                   1,1 1,2      1,1 1,3      1,2 1,3         |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|z*T_(1,1)*T_(1,2)})                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isHomogeneous Bmulti                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Dropping the internal grading (hom-degree only) breaks homogeneity because the
differential mixes different internal polynomial degrees of R:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : Bhomo = freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {1}, {1}, {3}})                         |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {Ring => R                                }                            |
|       Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                             |
|                                1,1   1,3   3,1                              |
|       Differential => null                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : DGAlgebra                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : setDiff(Bhomo, {x, y, z, x*T_(1,2)*T_(1,3) - y*T_(1,1)*T_(1,3) + z*T_(1|
|                                                                             |
|o11 = {Ring => R                                                      }      |
|       Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                             |
|                                1,1   1,3   3,1                              |
|       Differential => {x, y, z, z*T   T    - y*T   T    + x*T   T   }       |
|                                    1,1 1,2      1,1 1,3      1,2 1,3        |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : DGAlgebra                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|,1)*T_(1,2)})                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : isHomogeneous Bhomo                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = false                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The differential is set after construction (via *note setDiff: setDiff,) rather
than passed to freeDGAlgebra directly: the differential's ring is A.natural,
which does not exist until after the constructor runs.  For common DG algebras
arising in commutative algebra (Koszul complex, Tate resolution, acyclic
closure, etc.) dedicated constructors are available; see *note
koszulComplexDGA: koszulComplexDGA,, *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure,,
*note minimalModel: minimalModel,.

Caveat
======

There is currently a bug handling DG algebras that have no generators in some
homological degree but some in a later homological degree; for example
freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {5}}) may produce incorrect behavior if no hom-degree 3
generators are adjoined first.  The safer workflow is freeDGAlgebra with
hom-degrees only up to what is needed, followed by *note adjoinVariables:
adjoinVariables, to extend incrementally.

See also
========

  * *note koszulComplexDGA: koszulComplexDGA, -- The Koszul complex on the
    variables of a ring, as a DG algebra
  * *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, -- Tate's construction of a semifree
    acyclic DG algebra extension
  * *note minimalModel: minimalModel, -- Build the minimal DG algebra
    resolution of a quotient ring
  * *note adjoinVariables: adjoinVariables, -- Extend a DG algebra by a
    user-chosen list of cycles to be killed
  * *note setDiff: setDiff, -- Install or replace the differential on a DG
    algebra
  * *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra, -- The class of all DGAlgebras

