Description
===========

Routines that assemble a homology algebra — such as *note homologyAlgebra:
homologyAlgebra, and *note torAlgebra: torAlgebra, — must, in general, walk up
all homological degrees to find algebra generators.  When the DG algebra has
generators in even degree, that process is infinite; GenDegreeLimit caps the
search.  The answer is a truncation of the full homology algebra below the
specified degree, and is exact in the bounded case.

See also
========

  * *note RelDegreeLimit: RelDegreeLimit, -- Option to bound the homological
    degree searched for algebra relations
  * *note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, -- Compute the homology algebra of
    a DGAlgebra.
  * *note torAlgebra: torAlgebra, -- Computes the Tor algebra of a ring
  * *note findTrivialMasseyOperation: findTrivialMasseyOperation, -- Finds a
    trivial Massey operation on a set of generators of H(A)
  * *note isHomologyAlgebraTrivial: isHomologyAlgebraTrivial, -- Determines if
    the homology algebra of a DGAlgebra is trivial
  * *note isGolodHomomorphism: isGolodHomomorphism, -- Determines if the
    canonical map from the ambient ring is Golod

