getBasis(ZZ,Ring) -- Get a basis for a degree of a ring.
********************************************************

  * Function: *note getBasis: getBasis,
  * Usage: 
        M = getBasis(n,R)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Limit: getBasis_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value -1, Maximum number of basis elements to return from
        getBasis
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, The basis of the desired
        degree

Description
===========

This function was not meant for general use, but it fixes the first degree in
the degree tuple of the ring R, and finds a basis of that 'slice' of the ring.
It does this by using a cached version of the ring that forgets all other
degrees.  A Ring object in Macaulay2 will not have this cached ring by default,
but the rings used internally in the DGAlgebras package will.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note getBasis(ZZ,Ring): getBasis_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, -- Get a basis for a
    degree of a ring.
