HH DGAlgebra -- The homology algebra of a DG algebra
****************************************************

  * Function: *note homology: (Macaulay2Doc)homology,
  * Usage: 
        HA = homology A
        HA = HH A
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
  * Outputs:
      * HA, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the homology algebra HH_*(A), as
        a graded-commutative ring

Description
===========

Returns the homology algebra of A, caching the result inside A so subsequent
calls are fast.  This is a convenience wrapper around *note homologyAlgebra:
homologyAlgebra, that supports the HH shorthand.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c] / ideal(a^3, b^3, c^3, a^2*b^2*c^2)                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }                                   |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                                    |
|                               1,1   1,3                                     |
|      Differential => {a, b, c}                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : HA = HH A                                                               |
|Finding easy relations           :  -- used 0.0432544s (cpu); 0.041081s      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = HA                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|(thread); 0s (gc)                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : numgens HA                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 10                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : apply(maxDegree A + 1, i -> numgens prune homology(i, A))               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {1, 4, 6, 3}                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For DG algebras with even-degree generators (such as acyclic closures of
non-regular rings), call *note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, directly and
supply *note GenDegreeLimit: GenDegreeLimit, and *note RelDegreeLimit:
RelDegreeLimit, explicitly.

See also
========

  * *note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, -- Compute the homology algebra of
    a DGAlgebra.
  * *note zerothHomology: zerothHomology, -- The zeroth homology of a DG
    algebra as a ring
  * *note HH_ZZ DGAlgebra: HH_usZZ DGAlgebra, -- Computes the homology of a DG
    algebra as a module

