isAcyclic -- Determine whether a DG algebra has no higher homology
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isAcyc = isAcyclic A
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note EndDegree: isAcyclic_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEndDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value -1, Option to specify the degree to finish checking
        acyclicity
  * Outputs:
      * isAcyc, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if HH_i A =
        0 for all i > 0, and false otherwise

Description
===========

A DG algebra is acyclic (in the convention used by this package) if it has zero
homology in all positive degrees, so that A -> HH_0 A is a quasi-isomorphism.
isAcyclic checks homology degree by degree up through maxDegree A; for
unbounded DG algebras an *note EndDegree: EndDegree, option bounds the search.

The Koszul complex of a regular sequence is acyclic:

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]          |
|                                  |
|o1 = Q                            |
|                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing               |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^4, b^4, c^4, d^4)|
|                                  |
|             4   4   4   4        |
|o2 = ideal (a , b , c , d )       |
|                                  |
|o2 : Ideal of Q                   |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : isAcyclic(koszulComplexDGA I)|
|                                  |
|o3 = true                         |
+----------------------------------+

But the Koszul complex of a ring with nontrivial relations in homology is not:

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d] / ideal(a^4 + b^4 + c^4 + d^4)|
|                                                       |
|o4 = R                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isAcyclic(koszulComplexDGA R)                     |
|                                                       |
|o5 = false                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

An acyclic closure built to sufficient degree is acyclic in the checked range:

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d] / ideal(a^3, b^3, c^3, d^3)               |
|                                                                   |
|o6 = R                                                             |
|                                                                   |
|o6 : QuotientRing                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : A = acyclicClosure(R, EndDegree => 3)                         |
|                                                                   |
|o7 = {Ring => R                                                   }|
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                          |
|                               1,1   2,4                           |
|                                    2       2       2       2      |
|      Differential => {a, b, c, d, a T   , b T   , c T   , d T   } |
|                                      1,1     1,2     1,3     1,4  |
|                                                                   |
|o7 : DGAlgebra                                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isAcyclic(A, EndDegree => 3)                                  |
|                                                                   |
|o8 = true                                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra, -- The class of all DGAlgebras
  * *note HH_ZZ DGAlgebra: HH_usZZ DGAlgebra, -- Computes the homology of a DG
    algebra as a module
  * *note acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure, -- Tate's construction of a semifree
    acyclic DG algebra extension

