isGolodHomomorphism -- Determines if the canonical map from the ambient ring is Golod
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isGol = isGolodHomomorphism(R)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note GenDegreeLimit: isGolodHomomorphism_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmGenDegreeLimit
        =>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity, Maximum homological
        degree of generators used by isGolodHomomorphism
      * *note TMOLimit: isGolodHomomorphism_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTMOLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value infinity, Option to cap the arity of the
        trivial Massey operation used in isGolodHomomorphism
  * Outputs:
      * isGol, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This function determines if the canonical map from ambient R --> R is Golod.
It does this by computing an acyclic closure of ambient R (which is a *note
DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,), then tensors this with R, and determines if this DG
Algebra has a trivial Massey operation up to a certain homological degree
provided by the option GenDegreeLimit.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]/ideal{a^4+b^4+c^4+d^4}|
|                                               |
|o1 = R                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : QuotientRing                              |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isGolodHomomorphism(R,GenDegreeLimit=>5)  |
|                                               |
|o2 = true                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+

If R is a Golod ring, then ambient R $\rightarrow$ R is a Golod homomorphism.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]/ideal{a^4,b^4,c^4,d^4}          |
|                                                         |
|o3 = Q                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = Q/ideal (a^3*b^3*c^3*d^3)                       |
|                                                         |
|o4 = R                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isGolodHomomorphism(R,GenDegreeLimit=>5,TMOLimit=>3)|
|                                                         |
|o5 = true                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

The map from Q to R is Golod by a result of Avramov and Levin; we can only find
the trivial Massey operations out to a given degree.

