koszulComplexDGA(Ideal) -- The Koszul complex on the generators of an ideal, as a DG algebra
********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note koszulComplexDGA: koszulComplexDGA,
  * Usage: 
        A = koszulComplexDGA I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, An ideal of a ring R.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Variable: koszulComplexDGA, => ..., default value "T", The Koszul
        complex on the variables of a ring, as a DG algebra
  * Outputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, The Koszul
        complex over R on the chosen generators of I.

Description
===========

Given generators f_1, ..., f_r of I, the output is a DG algebra over R whose
underlying graded algebra is R[T_(1,1), ..., T_(1,r)] on r exterior generators
in hom-degree 1, with differential d(T_(1,i)) = f_i extended by the Leibniz
rule.  The variable naming convention and Variable option mirror *note
koszulComplexDGA(Ring): koszulComplexDGA,.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a, b, c]                      |
|                                              |
|o1 = R                                        |
|                                              |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                           |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^3, b^3, c^3, a^2 * b^2 * c^2)|
|                                              |
|             3   3   3   2 2 2                |
|o2 = ideal (a , b , c , a b c )               |
|                                              |
|o2 : Ideal of R                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = koszulComplexDGA I                   |
|                                              |
|o3 = {Ring => R                           }   |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]     |
|                               1,1   1,4      |
|                        3   3   3   2 2 2     |
|      Differential => {a , b , c , a b c }    |
|                                              |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                                |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : gens A.natural                           |
|                                              |
|o4 = {T   , T   , T   , T   }                 |
|       1,1   1,2   1,3   1,4                  |
|                                              |
|o4 : List                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : flatten entries matrix A.diff            |
|                                              |
|       3   3   3   2 2 2                      |
|o5 = {a , b , c , a b c , a, b, c}            |
|                                              |
|o5 : List                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+

The resulting complex coincides with *note koszul: (Macaulay2Doc)koszul,
applied to gens I, up to monomial order:

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : complexA = toComplex A                                  |
|                                                             |
|      1      4      6      4      1                          |
|o6 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                           |
|                                                             |
|     0      1      2      3      4                           |
|                                                             |
|o6 : Complex                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : ranks = apply(5, i -> numgens prune HH_i complexA)      |
|                                                             |
|o7 = {1, 3, 0, 0, 0}                                         |
|                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : ranks == apply(5, i -> numgens prune HH_i koszul gens I)|
|                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

In particular, I contains the redundant generator a^2 b^2 c^2 (it is in (a^3,
b^3, c^3)), so the Koszul complex is not exact at H_1; nonzero higher Koszul
homology encodes the relations and syzygies between the chosen generators.

See also
========

  * *note koszulComplexDGA(Ring): koszulComplexDGA, -- The Koszul complex on
    the variables of a ring, as a DG algebra
  * *note koszulComplexDGA(List): koszulComplexDGA_lpList_rp, -- The Koszul
    complex on a list of ring elements, as a DG algebra
  * *note HH_ZZ DGAlgebra: HH_usZZ DGAlgebra, -- Computes the homology of a DG
    algebra as a module

