koszulComplexDGA(List) -- The Koszul complex on a list of ring elements, as a DG algebra
****************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note koszulComplexDGA: koszulComplexDGA,
  * Usage: 
        A = koszulComplexDGA diffList
  * Inputs:
      * diffList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A nonempty list of *note
        RingElement: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement, s, all lying in a common ring
        R.  These become the images of the Koszul generators under the
        differential.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Variable: koszulComplexDGA, => ..., default value "T", The Koszul
        complex on the variables of a ring, as a DG algebra
  * Outputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, The Koszul
        complex over R on the sequence diffList.

Description
===========

This is the lowest-level form: the generators of I or R are replaced by an
arbitrary user-supplied list of ring elements.  Useful for building a Koszul
complex on a partial regular sequence or on arbitrary elements that may not
generate an ideal of interest.  The variable naming convention follows *note
koszulComplexDGA(Ring): koszulComplexDGA,: generators are named T_(1, j) with j
= 1, ..., #diffList.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y, z]                          |
|                                                  |
|o1 = R                                            |
|                                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = koszulComplexDGA({x^2, y*z})             |
|                                                  |
|o2 = {Ring => R                          }        |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]         |
|                               1,1   1,2          |
|                        2                         |
|      Differential => {x , y*z}                   |
|                                                  |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : gens A.natural                               |
|                                                  |
|o3 = {T   , T   }                                 |
|       1,1   1,2                                  |
|                                                  |
|o3 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : flatten entries matrix A.diff                |
|                                                  |
|       2                                          |
|o4 = {x , y*z, x, y, z}                           |
|                                                  |
|o4 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : apply(3, i -> numgens prune HH_i toComplex A)|
|                                                  |
|o5 = {1, 0, 0}                                    |
|                                                  |
|o5 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Here the sequence (x^2, y z) is regular in ZZ/101[x, y, z], so the Koszul
complex is acyclic in positive homology and H_0 is the quotient R/(x^2, y z)
(of dimension 1 as an R-module).

See also
========

  * *note koszulComplexDGA(Ring): koszulComplexDGA, -- The Koszul complex on
    the variables of a ring, as a DG algebra
  * *note koszulComplexDGA(Ideal): koszulComplexDGA_lpIdeal_rp, -- The Koszul
    complex on the generators of an ideal, as a DG algebra

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note koszulComplexDGA(List): koszulComplexDGA_lpList_rp, -- The Koszul
    complex on a list of ring elements, as a DG algebra
