ringMap -- The degree-zero ring map underlying a DGAlgebraMap
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        phi.ringMap

Description
===========

Every *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap, phi from A to B includes a key ringMap:
a *note RingMap: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap, from A.ring to B.ring giving the
restriction of phi to degree zero.  When the two DG algebras live over the same
ring, phi.ringMap is the identity; in general it is the degree-zero ring map
used to lift phi.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c]/ideal{a^3, b^3, c^3}                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = R / ideal{a^2*b^2*c^2}                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = acyclicClosure(R, EndDegree => 2)                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {Ring => R                                        }                     |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   ]                                    |
|                               1,1   2,3                                     |
|                                 2       2       2                           |
|      Differential => {a, b, c, a T   , b T   , c T   }                      |
|                                   1,1     1,2     1,3                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = acyclicClosure(S, EndDegree => 2)                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {Ring => S                                                              |
|      Underlying algebra => S[T   ..T   , T   ..T   , T   ..T   ]            |
|                               1,1   1,3   2,1   2,4   3,1   3,3             |
|                                 2       2       2         2 2       2 2     |
|      Differential => {a, b, c, a T   , b T   , c T   , a*b c T   , b c T   ,|
|                                   1,1     1,2     1,3         1,1       2,1 |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                     }                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|  2 2        2 2                                                             |
|-a b T   , -a c T   }                                                        |
|      2,3        2,2                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : phi = liftToDGMap(B, A, map(S, R))                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = map (S[T   ..T   , T   ..T   , T   ..T   ], R[T   ..T   ], {T   , T   , |
|             1,1   1,3   2,1   2,4   3,1   3,3      1,1   2,3     1,1   1,2  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : DGAlgebraMap                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|T   , T   , T   , T   , a, b, c})                                            |
| 1,3   2,1   2,2   2,3                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : phi.ringMap                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = map (S, R, {a, b, c})                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : RingMap S <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The ringMap is the bridge used internally by *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap,
to pushforward complexes between different rings.

See also
========

  * *note DGAlgebraMap: DGAlgebraMap, -- The class of DG algebra maps
  * *note liftToDGMap: liftToDGMap, -- Lift a ring homomorphism in degree zero
    to a DG algebra morphism
  * *note toComplexMap: toComplexMap, -- Construct the ComplexMap associated to
    a DGAlgebraMap

