setDiff -- Install or replace the differential on a DG algebra
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        A = setDiff(A, diffList)
        A = setDiff(A, diffList, InitializeComplex => false)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
      * diffList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of elements of
        A.natural, one per algebra generator, given in the same order as gens
        A.natural (which is the order of A.Degrees).  The i-th entry becomes
        d((gens A.natural)_i) and is extended to all of A.natural by
        R-linearity and the Leibniz rule. Each entry must have homological
        degree one less than its generator.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * InitializeComplex => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true, Whether to eagerly compute all differential
        matrices up to maxDegree A.  Defaults to true; set to false to skip the
        precomputation when only a low-degree fragment is needed.
      * InitializeDegreeZeroHomology => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, Whether to compute the
        quotient ring H_0(A) (needed by *note homologyAlgebra:
        homologyAlgebra,).  Defaults to true; set to false to skip the
        Grobner-basis computation when not needed.
  * Outputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, The same A, now
        with its diff field populated; returned for convenience in a chained
        call.

Description
===========

Because the ring A.natural does not exist until after *note freeDGAlgebra:
freeDGAlgebra, runs, the differential cannot be passed to the constructor and
must be set afterwards with setDiff. The list diffList supplies the image of
each algebra generator; Leibniz and R-linearity extend this to every element of
A.natural.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, y, z]                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {1}, {1}, {3}})                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {Ring => R                                }                             |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                              |
|                               1,1   1,3   3,1                               |
|      Differential => null                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : gens A.natural                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {T   , T   , T   , T   }                                                |
|       1,1   1,2   1,3   3,1                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : setDiff(A, {x, y, z, x*T_(1,2)*T_(1,3) - y*T_(1,1)*T_(1,3) + z*T_(1,1)*T|
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {Ring => R                                                      }       |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                              |
|                               1,1   1,3   3,1                               |
|      Differential => {x, y, z, z*T   T    - y*T   T    + x*T   T   }        |
|                                   1,1 1,2      1,1 1,3      1,2 1,3         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|_(1,2)})                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : flatten entries matrix A.diff                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {x, y, z, z*T   T    - y*T   T    + x*T   T   , x, y, z}                |
|                  1,1 1,2      1,1 1,3      1,2 1,3                          |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here d(T_(1,i)) = x_i (so the Koszul piece on T_(1,*) is installed) and
d(T_(3,1)) is the Koszul-relation 2-cycle x T_(1,2) T_(1,3) - y T_(1,1) T_(1,3)
+ z T_(1,1) T_(1,2), turning A into a Tate-resolution fragment for R/(x, y, z).
Converting to a *note Complex: (Complexes)Complex, shows the installed
differentials:

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Acomplex = toComplex A                      |
|                                                 |
|      1      3      3      2      3      3      1|
|o6 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R |
|                                                 |
|     0      1      2      3      4      5      6 |
|                                                 |
|o6 : Complex                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Acomplex.dd_1                               |
|                                                 |
|o7 = | x y z |                                   |
|                                                 |
|             1      3                            |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                             |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Acomplex.dd_2                               |
|                                                 |
|o8 = | -y -z 0  |                                |
|     | x  0  -z |                                |
|     | 0  x  y  |                                |
|                                                 |
|             3      3                            |
|o8 : Matrix R  <-- R                             |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Validity.  The package does not check that the installed differential squares
to zero; a user-supplied diffList that violates d^2 = 0 yields a malformed DG
algebra with silently wrong downstream behavior.  The chain-map conditions can
be checked after the fact via *note isWellDefined(DGAlgebra):
isWellDefined_lpDGAlgebra_rp,.

Options.  InitializeComplex controls whether setDiff eagerly builds all
differential matrices up to maxDegree A (the sum of the hom-degrees of the
odd-hom-degree generators).  Set it to false to defer this computation when
only low-degree information is needed:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Abig = freeDGAlgebra(R, {{1}, {1}, {1}, {3}})                           |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = {Ring => R                                }                             |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                              |
|                               1,1   1,3   3,1                               |
|      Differential => null                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : setDiff(Abig, {x, y, z, x*T_(1,2)*T_(1,3) - y*T_(1,1)*T_(1,3) + z*T_(1,|
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {Ring => R                                                      }      |
|       Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ]                             |
|                                1,1   1,3   3,1                              |
|       Differential => {x, y, z, z*T   T    - y*T   T    + x*T   T   }       |
|                                    1,1 1,2      1,1 1,3      1,2 1,3        |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : DGAlgebra                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|1)*T_(1,2)}, InitializeComplex => false)                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

InitializeDegreeZeroHomology controls whether the quotient ring H_0(A) = A_0 /
image(d_1) is computed on the spot (a Grobner-basis computation, deferred to
*note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, if turned off).  Default: true.  Turn
it off if you have many hom-degree-1 generators and are not about to compute HH
A as a DG algebra.

Caveat
======

The order of entries in diffList must match the order of generators in gens
A.natural (equivalently, of A.Degrees).  For constructors that adjoin
generators incrementally (*note adjoinVariables: adjoinVariables,, *note
acyclicClosure: acyclicClosure,, *note killCycles: killCycles,), the new
generators come after all existing ones in this ordering.

See also
========

  * *note freeDGAlgebra: freeDGAlgebra, -- Construct a free DG algebra with
    given generator degrees
  * *note koszulComplexDGA: koszulComplexDGA, -- The Koszul complex on the
    variables of a ring, as a DG algebra
  * *note adjoinVariables: adjoinVariables, -- Extend a DG algebra by a
    user-chosen list of cycles to be killed
  * *note isWellDefined(DGAlgebra): isWellDefined_lpDGAlgebra_rp, -- Check that
    a DG algebra has correct structure and a differential that squares to zero
  * *note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, -- Compute the homology algebra of
    a DGAlgebra.

Ways to use setDiff:
====================

  * "setDiff(DGAlgebra,List)"
  * *note setDiff(DGModule,List): setDiff_lpDGModule_cmList_rp, -- Install the
    list of generator differentials on a free DG module

For the programmer
==================

The object *note setDiff: setDiff, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

