torAlgebra -- Computes the Tor algebra of a ring
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        torR = torAlgebra(R)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note GenDegreeLimit: torAlgebra_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmGenDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity, Maximum homological degree
        searched for Tor-algebra generators
      * *note RelDegreeLimit: torAlgebra_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmRelDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity, Maximum homological degree
        searched for Tor-algebra relations
  * Outputs:
      * torR, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]                           |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : TorR = torAlgebra(R)                          |
|                                                   |
|o2 = TorR                                          |
|                                                   |
|o2 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = R/ideal{a^3,b^3,c^3,d^5}                  |
|                                                   |
|o3 = S                                             |
|                                                   |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : TorS = torAlgebra(S, GenDegreeLimit => 3)     |
|                                                   |
|o4 = TorS                                          |
|                                                   |
|o4 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+

The above example calculates the Tor algebra of R and S up to degree 3, by
default.  One can also specify the maximum degree to compute generators of the
Tor algebra by specifying the GenDegreeLimit option.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]/ideal{a^3,b^3,c^3,d^3,a^2*b^2*c^3*d^2}|
|                                                               |
|o5 = R                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                              |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : TorR = torAlgebra(R,GenDegreeLimit=>5)                    |
|                                                               |
|o6 = TorR                                                      |
|                                                               |
|o6 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

