torAlgebra(Ring,Ring) -- Computes Tor_R(S,k) up to a specified generating and relating degree.
**********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note torAlgebra: torAlgebra,
  * Usage: 
        TorRS = torAlgebra(R,S,GenDegreeLimit=>m,RelDegreeLimit=>n)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note GenDegreeLimit: torAlgebra_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmGenDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity, Maximum homological degree
        searched for Tor-algebra generators
      * *note RelDegreeLimit: torAlgebra_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmRelDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity, Maximum homological degree
        searched for Tor-algebra relations
  * Outputs:
      * TorRS, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d]/ideal{a^4,b^4,c^4,d^4}                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker matrix {{a^3*b^3*c^3*d^3}};                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = R/ideal{a^3*b^3*c^3*d^3}                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : HB = torAlgebra(R,S,GenDegreeLimit=>4,RelDegreeLimit=>8)                |
|Finding easy relations           :  -- used 0.675941s (cpu); 0.557274s       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = HB                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|(thread); 0s (gc)                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : numgens HB                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 35                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : apply(5,i -> #(flatten entries getBasis(i,HB)))                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {1, 1, 4, 10, 20}                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Mres = freeResolution(M, LengthLimit=>8)                                |
|                                                                             |
|      1      1      4      10      20      35      56      84      120       |
|o7 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R          |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2      3       4       5       6       7       8          |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that in this example, $Tor_*^R(S,k)$ has trivial multiplication, since the
map from R to S is a Golod homomorphism by a theorem of Levin and Avramov.

