zerothHomology -- The zeroth homology of a DG algebra as a ring
***************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        HA0 = zerothHomology A
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DGAlgebra: DGAlgebra,, 
  * Outputs:
      * HA0, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, HH_0(A), presented as a
        quotient of A.ring

Description
===========

Returns HH_0(A) as a ring, computed by taking A.ring modulo the image of the
degree-one part of the differential.  For a Koszul complex KR =
koszulComplexDGA I over R, this recovers the quotient ring R/I.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = ZZ/101[x,y,z]                    |
|                                          |
|o1 = Q                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, y^2, z^2, x*y*z)      |
|                                          |
|             2   2   2                    |
|o2 = ideal (x , y , z , x*y*z)            |
|                                          |
|o2 : Ideal of Q                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : KQ = koszulComplexDGA I              |
|                                          |
|o3 = {Ring => Q                          }|
|      Underlying algebra => Q[T   ..T   ] |
|                               1,1   1,4  |
|                        2   2   2         |
|      Differential => {x , y , z , x*y*z} |
|                                          |
|o3 : DGAlgebra                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : H0 = zerothHomology KQ               |
|                                          |
|o4 = H0                                   |
|                                          |
|o4 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : describe H0                          |
|                                          |
|              Q                           |
|o5 = -------------------                  |
|       2   2   2                          |
|     (z , y , x , x*y*z)                  |
+------------------------------------------+

When A is an acyclic closure, zerothHomology A returns the quotient ring on
which the DG algebra resolves the residue field.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = Q / I                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : A = acyclicClosure(R, EndDegree => 2)                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {Ring => R                                                              |
|      Underlying algebra => R[T   ..T   , T   ..T   , T   ..T   ]            |
|                               1,1   1,3   2,1   2,4   3,1   3,3             |
|      Differential => {x, y, z, x*T   , y*T   , z*T   , y*z*T   , y*z*T   ,  |
|                                   1,1     1,2     1,3       1,1       2,1   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : DGAlgebra                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                             }                                               |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-y*z*T   T   , -y*z*T   T   }                                                |
|      1,1 1,3        1,1 1,2                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : zerothHomology A                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|      ZZ                                                                     |
|o8 = ---                                                                     |
|     101                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note HH DGAlgebra: HH DGAlgebra, -- The homology algebra of a DG algebra
  * *note homologyAlgebra: homologyAlgebra, -- Compute the homology algebra of
    a DGAlgebra.

Ways to use zerothHomology:
===========================

  * "zerothHomology(DGAlgebra)"

